ktrees' symlink). The name used to be \"$CORE_NAME-$$\", but an\n# agent's sandboxed shell runs in its own PID namespace where $$ is 2 or 3\n# for every agent, so siblings wrote into one dir and wiped each other's\n# checks mid-SBY (V2 incident 03). mktemp gives a unique name instead.\n# FORMAL_WORK_ID pins the suffix so tools/eval/formal.py can remove exactly\n# its own dir afterwards. genchecks.py derives @core\n…[23390 of 26462 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b2dd3599d2317edb]…\ncosim for a single ELF using the run_cosim script.\"\"\"\ntools/eval/cosim.py:54:            [sys.executable, str(worktree_path / \"test/cosim/run_cosim.py\"),\ntools/eval/cosim.py:73:    Full-trace cosim would take >30 min; the CRC guard is sensitive to any\ntools/eval/cosim.py:76:    cross-checks it at the cosim stage too.\ntools/eval/cosim.py:79:    # projects that only run cosim.\ntools/eval/cosim.py:125:def run_cosim(worktree: str, target: str | None = None) -> dict:\ntools/eval/cosim.py:130:                cosim_sim from cores/<target>/obj_dir/cosim_sim instead of\ntools/eval/cosim.py:131:                the default test/cosim/obj_dir/cosim_sim, and injects\ntools/eval/cosim.py:143:    obj_dir = Path(env.get(\"OBJ_DIR\", \"test/cosim/obj_dir\"))\ntools/eval/cosim.py:146:    sim_bin = str(obj_dir / \"cosim_sim\")\ntools/eval/cosim.py:148:    # Split ELFs into full-trace cosim vs CRC-validated coremark.\ntools/eval/cosim.py:156:    # 1. Full-trace cosim of small ELFs (parallel).\ntools/eval/cosim.py:184:    result = run_cosim(\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
