{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'for p in /AGENTS.md /srv/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep1/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/AGENTS.md /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-astra_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/AGENTS.md; do if test -f \"$p\"; then cat \"$p\"; fi; done; rg --files --hidden -g AGENTS.md -g '\"'\"'!'\"\\\\.git' -g '\"'!*coremark*'\"'; cat Makefile cores/bench/core.yaml formal/run_all.sh\"", "aggregated_output": ".PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\n.DEFAULT_GOAL := help\n\n# Resolve OSS CAD Suite path so commands work even when the user hasn't\n# sourced .toolchain/oss-cad-suite/environment in this shell.\nTOOLCHAIN_DIR := $(CURDIR)/.toolchain\nOSS_BIN       := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/oss-cad-suite/bin\nLOCAL_BIN     := $(TOOLCHAIN_DIR)/bin\nexport PATH := $(OSS_BIN):$(LOCAL_BIN):$(PATH)\n\n# Orchestrator knobs (pass-through to tools.orchestrator):\n#   N        — number of rounds for `make loop` (default 10).\n#   K        — tournament size, slots per round (default 1 = sequential).\n#   AGENT    — codex (default) or claude. Honors a pre-existing\n#              AGENT_PROVIDER env var if AGENT isn't set on the make\n#              command line.\n#   BASE     — when forking a new TARGET, copy from cores/<BASE>/.\n#              Default: baseline (orchestrator-side default).\n#   COREMARK — target CoreMark iterations/sec (e.g. '370').\n#   LUT      — target LUT count (e.g. '3000').\n#   WORKTREE — default ON. `make loop` first creates a dedicated git worktree\n#              at .worktrees/<TARGET>/ on branch core-<TARGET> and re-execs\n#              itself there. Lets two `make loop` invocations for different\n#              TARGETs run in parallel without git index/merge collisions.\n#              To opt out (run directly on the current branch + cwd) pass\n#              an explicit empty value: `make loop TARGET=v1 WORKTREE=`.\nN        ?= 10\nK        ?= 1\nAGENT    ?= $(or $(AGENT_PROVIDER),codex)\nBASE     ?=\nCOREMARK ?=\nLUT      ?=\nWORKTREE ?= 1\n\n# Compose optional CLI flags for the orchestrator. Empty vars produce\n# empty strings so the orchestrator falls back to its defaults.\nORCH_FLAGS  = --iterations $(N) --tournament-size $(K)\nifneq ($(strip $(BASE)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --base $(BASE)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(COREMARK)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --coremark-target $(COREMARK)\nendif\nifneq ($(strip $(LUT)),)\n  ORCH_FLAGS += --lut-target $(LUT)\nendif\n\n# Multi-core: TARGET selects the core under cores/<TARGET>\n…[15718 of 18790 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1e0c3ffa968703eb]…\nheses make the assumption satisfiable, so this\n        # branch never matches and the regular DONE (PASS branch covers it.\n        PASS=$((PASS+1))\n    else\n        FAIL=$((FAIL+1)); FAILED+=(\"$name\")\n    fi\ndone\nTOTAL=$((PASS+FAIL))\nif [ $TOTAL -eq 0 ]; then\n    FAIL=1\n    FAILED+=(\"no_checks_generated\")\nfi\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Formal: $PASS passed, $FAIL failed\"\nif [ $FAIL -gt 0 ]; then\n    echo \"Failed: ${FAILED[*]}\"\n    # Surface the FIRST failing check's logfile tail. tools/eval/formal.py\n    # captures this script's stdout/stderr into formal['detail'] and the\n    # orchestrator now records that in experiments/log.jsonl, so what we\n    # print here is what shows up as the diagnostic for the failed run.\n    first=\"${FAILED[0]}\"\n    if [ -f \"$first/logfile.txt\" ]; then\n        echo \"\"\n        echo \"--- $first/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\"\n        tail -30 \"$first/logfile.txt\"\n    fi\n    echo \"\"\n    echo \"Full run log: $LOG\"\n    echo \"Per-check logs in: $CORE_DIR/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\"\nfi\n[ $FAIL -eq 0 ]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
