 At each step form the 34-bit trial\n  value T={R[31:0], next_two_dividend_bits}. Compute T-D, T-2D, and T-3D in\n  parallel as explicitly unsigned 35-bit subtractions. The top subtraction\n  bit indicates underflow; use it directly instead of placing a separate\n  comparison before subtraction. Select the largest non-underflowing\n  multiple, ap\n…[1873 of 4945 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:36e5116360eb608f]…\nons with\n      a shared, fully combinational 16-step radix-4 unsigned quotient and\n      remainder network, signed magnitude conversion, and RV32M corner-case\n      result selection as specified above. Use explicitly widened parallel\n      trial subtractions and borrow-derived digit selection. Preserve the\n      op/a/b/out interface, ALTOPS branch, multiplier, and RV32I behavior.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve existing tests and add deterministic reference comparisons for\n      all four division/remainder operations using integer truncation toward\n      zero. Exercise all sign combinations, zero divisors, INT_MIN/-1,\n      unsigned high-bit operands, divisors 1 and powers of two, a<b, a=b,\n      maximum values, and cases that exercise radix-4 quotient digits 0..3\n      and cross the D/2D/3D selection boundaries. Add seeded randomized full\n      32-bit operand coverage and back-to-back operation changes to detect\n      width, sign, digit selection, and combinational-state errors.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
