{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json,re\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('.tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261001-003-r1s2.log')\nfor line in p.read_text().splitlines():\n try: d=json.loads(line)\n except ValueError: continue\n if d.get('type') \"'!= '\"'item.completed': continue\n i=d.get('item',{})\n if i.get('type')=='agent_message': print(i.get('text',''))\n elif i.get('type')=='command_execution':\n  out=i.get('aggregated_output','')\n  matches=[s for s in out.splitlines() if re.search(r'(CoreMark.*(?:cycle|CRC)|cycles[=: ]+[0-9]|[0-9]+ cycles|Fmax [0-9]|iterations[=: ]+[0-9]|fitness[=: ]+[0-9])',s,re.I)]\n  if matches: print('\\\\n'.join(matches)[:4000])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json,re\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('.tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261001-003-r1s2.log')\nfor line in p.read_text().splitlines():\n try: d=json.loads(line)\n except ValueError: continue\n if d.get('type') \"'!= '\"'item.completed': continue\n i=d.get('item',{})\n if i.get('type')=='agent_message': print(i.get('text',''))\n elif i.get('type')=='command_execution':\n  out=i.get('aggregated_output','')\n  matches=[s for s in out.splitlines() if re.search(r'(CoreMark.*(?:cycle|CRC)|cycles[=: ]+[0-9]|[0-9]+ cycles|Fmax [0-9]|iterations[=: ]+[0-9]|fitness[=: ]+[0-9])',s,re.I)]\n  if matches: print('\\\\n'.join(matches)[:4000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "I’ll implement the predictor and saved prediction bit, add directed stall/recovery tests, then run lint, formal, cosimulation, and Gowin timing within the time budget.\n\n\t@echo \"  make fpga TARGET=v1     — FPGA fitness eval (Gowin Fmax + CoreMark cycles)\"\n\tAGENT_PROVIDER=$(AGENT) python3 -m tools.orchestrator $(subst --iterations $(N),--iterations 1,$(ORCH_FLAGS)) $(ORCH_TARGET_FLAG)\nasync def _run(dut, program, dmem_init=None, max_cycles=200):\n    rets, _ = await _run(dut, program, max_cycles=20)\nThe predictor RTL passes lint. Recovery and training are gated by EX advancement, so an older dmem stall holds the instruction and its prediction bit intact. I’m starting formal checks and adding tests for correct predictions, loop exits, aliasing, and stalled recovery.\n\nasync def _run(dut, program, dmem_init=None, max_cycles=200):\n  2. CoreMark CRC validation via the sim's UART capture — full-trace cosim\ndef run_coremark_crc(coremark_elf: Path, sim_bin: str, worktree: str, env: dict | None = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Run coremark.elf on the sim and validate UART-reported CRC.\n    computational bug since CoreMark's CRC is computed over every algorithm's\n        return {'passed': False, 'elf': coremark_elf.name, 'field': 'crc_mismatch',\n    # 2. CoreMark CRC validation (sequential — runs the 500M-cycle sim).\n        cm_result = run_coremark_crc(coremark, sim_bin, worktree, env)\n    \"\"\"Require CoreMark's own validation and exact expected CRC markers,\n    Verilator CoreMark run (with random memory stalls) for cycles.\n        'ipc_coremark': float,           — iter/cycle\nThe existing unit suite and selftest/CoreMark cosimulation pass. The cosim build needed `NRET=1` to match `core.yaml`; the core’s single-channel RVFI ports are unchanged. I’m starting the three-placement Gowin evaluation while extending the directed tests.\n\ndef run_verilator(sim_bin, elf, maxcycles=50_000_000, timeout=120, sim_flags=()):\n        'ipc_coremark':  round(cm['iter_per_cycle'], 6),\nFormal passed all 53 checks. The first full evaluation measured 4,202,246 CoreMark cycles and 5.204 MHz median Fmax, giving fitness 12.38—below the required 12.67752. I’m simplifying the counter update circuit to reduce predictor area and routing while keeping the same 128-entry, two-bit behavior.\n\nThe directed tests now pass, including both saved branch directions during five-cycle dmem stalls, recovery with imem unavailable, 512-byte index collisions, reset after training, and exact RVFI comparison against the existing ISS. The counter-update revision is still running through formal and Gowin.\n\nThe revised predictor measured 13.32 fitness: 4,202,246 CoreMark cycles at 5.596 MHz median Gowin Fmax. That exceeds 12.67752 and is about 9.9% above 12.12. Final verification is still running; I also fixed the file-order issue in the requested wildcard lint command.\n\nplace_option 0: Fmax 5.226 MHz, 156 logic levels; logic 12917, registers 718, LUT-RAM 8, BSRAM 6, DSP 6\nFinal unit tests, cosimulation, and standalone Gowin timing pass. One formal check remains: register consistency (`reg_ch0`); the other 52 have passed. I’m waiting for that result before completing the validati