{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_61", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r10s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r10s0',\n'title':'Remove phase-enable muxes from feed-forward divider banks',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.44 at median Gowin Fmax 73.790 MHz and\n4,230,003 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Prior divider work already\nreplaced shared feedback with dedicated predecessor-to-successor\nquotient/remainder banks, but every bank still has an iteration-decoded\nhold enable. The divider is now feed-forward internally: a later phase\nnever feeds an earlier one. The real result is observed only after all\nseven register transfers. These per-phase hold muxes therefore need\nnot lie after the arithmetic. Recent branch-only changes and launch\nretiming did not clear the acceptance margin; simplify the existing\nbank register inputs without changing the recurrence or schedule.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Make quotient_bank[1:7] and remainder_bank[1:7] advance every clock\noutside reset. Remove only the per-phase active_q && \"'!complete_q &&\niteration_q==p write enable around these banks. Keep their static\npredecessor wiring, prefix widths, radix-4 trial subtractions, large-D\nbypass and next-value expressions exactly as in the champion. This is\none local register-enable micro-optimization, not a divider latency or\npipeline-depth change. Keep bank zero and all operand/sign metadata\ncaptured only on start && !busy.\n\nThe correctness argument is a wavefront through a feed-forward chain.\nAt launch, bank zero receives the two-bit normalized prefix. On the\nnext edge phase zero produces the correct eight-bit prefix in bank\none; on each following edge one more bank becomes correct. By the\nedge that sets iteration_q to seven, bank seven contains the same\n32-bit unsigned quotient/remainder as before. Earlier banks may be\nrecomputed, but their inputs do not change during the active request,\nso once a bank is correct it stays correct. Values in not-yet-ready\nbanks are speculative and never consumed as an architectural result.\n\nPreserve the existing full-width triple_divisor_q preparation on the\nfirst active recurrence edge. Its new-request value is ready before\nphase one must produce bank two. Earlier speculative phase-one work\nmay use an old multiple but is overwritten before that bank'\"'s scheduled\nobservation. Each following phase similarly receives a correct prefix\nbefore its scheduled use. The launch divisor, signs and bank-zero\nvalues remain stable until the current request is accepted. Keep the\nexisting local phase-zero 3D expression; this proposal does not add\narithmetic to the launch path or relocate divisor-multiple registers.\n\nKeep active_q, complete_q, iteration_q, start, busy, done, accept,\nresult_q and the result mux unchanged. In particular, hold completion\nthrough result_q when accept is low, retain the original nine-cycle EX\noccupancy and match real and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS scheduling exactly.\nReset still clears every bank and all control state. No bank register\nmay accidentally become combinational, and no execution phase is\nremoved. Keep divide-by-zero quotient/remainder, INT_MIN/-1, signed\ntruncation and remainder sign, all four RV32M operations and ALTOPS\nformulas unchanged. Preserve EX operand capture, forwarding, memory\nbackpressure, decode legality, nret=1 IO and strict RVFI retirement.\n\nThe intended benefit is removal of the feedback/enable selection after\neach phase's subtract-and-select cone, together with reduced fanout\nfrom the iteration decode. It uses the same number of arithmetic and\nquotient/remainder registers and adds no cycles. Extra speculative\nswitching is possible before the valid wavefront settles; synthesis\nmapping, routing and the unchanged EX/address cones may limit Fmax.\nInspect vendor reports to confirm the per-phase feedback muxes disappear.\n\nForecast an unmeasured six percent fitness gain with low confidence.\nCoreMark should retain exactly 4,230,003 bracketed cycles with the same\nstall sequence. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 182.46424,\ncorresponding to about 77.183 MHz. Use all three Gowin placement options\nand unchanged CoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker gates, not a single local\npath improvement. Keep the standard formal and RVFI cosimulation gates;\nALTOPS alone cannot establish real divider arithmetic correctness.\n\nPreserve the existing divider tests that check each scheduled unsigned\nprefix against an independent integer reference, exact done timing,\nsource changes while busy, reset cancellation and held completion. Add\nback-to-back requests with sharply different divisor magnitudes and\nsigns so stale speculative prefixes and the prior request's 3D cannot\nescape. Check a normal division immediately after zero-divisor and\nINT_MIN/-1 cases, and vice versa, with accept held low across completion.\nDo not demand inactive speculative banks retain their former values;\ncontinue checking every bank when its result is scheduled to be valid,\nand all architectural outputs, ordering and progress without relaxing\nany assertion about valid execution.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'''Remove the iteration-qualified clock enable only from the seven\nsuccessor quotient/remainder bank register pairs, so their existing\nnext-value equations run every non-reset edge. Preserve reset, launch\nbank, divisor and sign capture, 3D preparation, arithmetic widths,\nlarge-divisor bypass, ALTOPS, count/done/accept and held-result logic.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'''Retain scheduled-prefix, exact-latency and RV32M reference checks.\nAdd consecutive requests with contrasting divisors/signs, exceptions,\nbusy input changes and delayed acceptance to expose stale speculative\nbank or 3D values. Preserve reset-at-every-iteration coverage and\ncheck final data stability throughout a blocked completion.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all existing assertions and cycle checks. Exercise consecutive\nDIV/REM variants, immediately dependent consumers, multiply/load\nneighbors, reset and simultaneous imem/dmem stalls. Verify unchanged\nRVFI operands/results/order, exact-once retirement and nine-cycle\nexecution occupancy while older memory work drains.\n'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88,default_flow_style=False))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised hypothesis is schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
