{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r10s0.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Remove hold muxes only from feed-forward divider remainder banks'\nd['motivation']='''The champion scores 174.44 at median Gowin Fmax 73.790 MHz and\n4,230,003 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Prior divider work established\ndedicated predecessor-to-successor quotient/remainder banks, but every\nbank still has an iteration-decoded hold enable after its arithmetic.\nThe remainder path is now feed-forward, and each scheduled result is\nobserved only after its required register transfers. Remove unnecessary\nhold selection from these arithmetic-result registers. Keep the quotient\nshift-register enables: an isolated broader experiment that removed both\nsets of enables passed behavioral tests but inferred five extra LUT RAMs\nand fell to 65.596 MHz. The narrower proposal targets the remainder cone\nwhile preserving the champion's quotient storage behavior.\n'''\nh=d['hypothesis']\nh=h.replace('Make quotient_bank[1:7] and remainder_bank[1:7] advance every clock\\\\noutside reset. Remove only the per-phase active_q && \"'!complete_q &&'\"\\\\niteration_q==p write enable around these banks.', 'Make only remainder_bank[1:7] advance every clock outside reset.\\\\nSplit the existing bank always_ff block into two blocks: quotient banks\\\\nretain their exact reset and active_q && \"'!complete_q && iteration_q==p'\"\\\\nenable, while remainder banks retain reset and otherwise unconditionally\\\\ncapture the same next-remainder expression.')\nh=h.replace('Earlier banks may be\\\\nrecomputed, but their inputs do not change during the active request,\\\\nso once a bank is correct it stays correct.', 'An earlier remainder bank may be recomputed, but once its predecessor\\\\nquotient/remainder pair is correct, those inputs stay correct during the\\\\nrequest. Its newly computed remainder therefore stays correct as well.\\\\nEach quotient bank is written on its original scheduled edge using the\\\\nthen-correct predecessor remainder; no quotient timing changes.')\nh=h.replace('removal of the feedback/enable selection after\\\\neach phase\\\\'s subtract-and-select cone, together with reduced fanout\\\\nfrom the iteration decode.', 'removal of the remainder feedback/enable selection after\\\\neach phase\\\\'s subtract-and-select cone, together with reduced load on\\\\nthe iteration decode. Keep quotient enables even though their removal\\\\nwould also be functionally legal, to avoid remapping quotient shifts\\\\ninto additional LUT-RAM structures as seen in the broader experiment.')\nh=h.replace('Inspect vendor reports to confirm the per-phase feedback muxes disappear.', 'Inspect vendor reports to confirm the remainder hold muxes disappear\\\\nand the quotient banks retain their original enabled register mapping.')\nd['hypothesis']=h\nd['changes'][0]['description']='''Split each phase's quotient/remainder register block. Keep the\nquotient reset, write enable and next-value logic exactly unchanged.\nGive the successor remainder bank its own always_ff block with the\nsame reset and an unconditional non-reset assignment of its existing\nlarge_d-selected next value. Preserve bank zero, divisor/sign capture,\n3D preparation, arithmetic, ALTOPS, count/done/accept and held-result logic.\n'''\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,data):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Schema-valid revised remainder-bank hypothesis')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
