{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"agent_message","text":"The remainder-only variant also preserves behavior but misses the timing target. Its worst path reveals a more direct target: branch resolution feeds prospective register-write qualification, although conditional branches never write a register. I’ll use that as the final hypothesis—remove this redundant dependency while preserving branch traps."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_78", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil,yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/867d4c2f/21267d59/branch_write_qual')\nfor d in ('rtl','test'): shutil.copytree(Path('cores/bench')/d,p/d,dirs_exist_ok=True)\nf=p/'rtl/ex_stage.sv';s=f.read_text()\nold=\\\"\\\"\\\"    if (misalign_fault) begin\n      ctrl_with_trap.is_illegal = 1'b1;\n      ctrl_with_trap.reg_write  = 1'b0;\n    end\\\"\\\"\\\"\nnew=\\\"\\\"\\\"    if (misalign_fault) begin\n      ctrl_with_trap.is_illegal = 1'b1;\n    end\n    if (misalign_jump) ctrl_with_trap.reg_write = 1'b0;\\\"\\\"\\\"\nassert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new);f.write_text(s)\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r10s0',\n'title':'Remove branch-direction feedback from prospective write qualification',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.44 at 73.790 MHz and 4,230,003 CoreMark\ncycles. Recent micro_opt branch-comparison rewrites failed to clear the\nacceptance margin. Detailed Gowin reports from isolated local trials\nexpose a WB-to-EX-to-forwarding-to-ID path as well as EX-to-PC paths.\nIn ex_stage, misalign_fault includes the full forwarded branch predicate\nand suppresses ctrl_with_trap.reg_write. That flag also drives\nnext_reg_write and prospective source-mask generation in decode.\nConditional branches already have reg_write=0 from validated decode,\nso their direction and target alignment unnecessarily enter this\nregister-write qualification cone. Use that exact instruction-class\ninvariant to remove the false control dependency.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Separate EX trap reporting from destination-write suppression by\ninstruction class. Keep misalign_branch, misalign_jump and misalign_fault\nexactly unchanged, including their full branch/jump predicates and target\nalignment checks. Initialize ctrl_with_trap from in.ctrl as today, set\nctrl_with_trap.is_illegal when misalign_fault is true, but clear\nctrl_with_trap.reg_write only when misalign_jump is true. In concrete\nterms, move the reg_write=0 assignment out of the if(misalign_fault)\nblock and place it under a separate if(misalign_jump). Keep\nnext_reg_write = in.valid && ctrl_with_trap.reg_write unchanged.\n\nThis relies on a property of the existing decoder, not a new assumption:\nevery reachable ctrl with is_branch=1 has reg_write=0. Both legal\nconditional branches and reserved branch encodings cannot write an rd;\nreserved encodings retain the default illegal controls. Therefore\nin.ctrl.reg_write && \"'!misalign_fault is architecturally identical to\nin.ctrl.reg_write && !misalign_jump for every reachable instruction.\nA taken misaligned branch still reports a trap and has no destination\nwrite, since the decoded write flag was already zero. A misaligned JAL\nor JALR still loses its link-register write. Aligned jumps, ordinary ALU\noperations and all M-extension operations keep their original write flags.\nKeep every illegal-decoder default and validated opcode/funct arm intact.\n\nThe timing opportunity is specific: remove the 32-bit forwarded branch\ncomparison, branch-taken logic and branch-target qualification from the\nwrite-enable signal used by prospective forwarding. The shorter signal\ncontinues through the existing younger/older tag matches and registered\nsource masks. This reduces a late EX-to-ID feedback path and the fanout\nof the branch predicate without changing comparator arithmetic, source\npriority, prediction, stages, instruction latency or recovery timing.\nNo additional registers or timing constraints are needed.\n\nLeave actual_taken, redirect, redirect_target, predictor training,\npc_next, branch metadata and all fault reporting unchanged. Do not\nsuppress branch misalignment traps or redirect a faulting branch. Keep\nmemory misalignment handling in MEM, x0 exclusion, trap-qualified jump\nforwarding, load/multiply bubbles, division capture/completion, retained\nWB forwarding during dmem stalls, all ready/hold priorities, nret=1 IO\nand exact retirement ordering. Leave real multiply/divide and ALTOPS\nformulas and scheduling unchanged. Do not apply the simplification to\narbitrary unconstrained control-bit combinations: prove it through the\nunchanged instruction decoder and full-core formal model.\n\nForecast an unmeasured six percent fitness gain with low confidence.\nOther EX-to-PC, general-ALU/address and divider paths may limit the gain;\nthis is a targeted control-cone hypothesis rather than a demonstrated\nfitness improvement. At unchanged 4,230,003 CoreMark cycles, acceptance\nrequires fitness above 182.46424, about 77.183 MHz median Gowin Fmax.\nMeasure all three placement options and retain the unchanged canonical\nCoreMark CRC/UART/bounds/marker checks. Run standard formal and RVFI\ncosimulation; verify the branch comparison no longer feeds prospective\nregister-write qualification in the vendor netlist.\n\nKeep all existing tests and add a decoder property that every legal\nconditional branch has is_branch=1 and reg_write=0, while reserved branch\nfunct3 values stay illegal and side-effect-free. Test taken and untaken\nmisaligned branches of all six conditions with both forwarding operands,\nand branch instruction bits[11:7] deliberately matching the following\ninstruction'\"'s source so a spurious prospective writer is detected.\nCheck aligned/misaligned JAL and JALR link writes, including a younger\nconsumer of the suppressed rd, older/younger same-rd priority and held\nMEM/WB data under simultaneous bus stalls. Check identical RVFI traps,\nsource operands, destination writes, next PCs and ordered retirements.\nPreserve every existing assertion and exact-cycle/progress check.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Continue reporting branch or jump misalignment through is_illegal,\nbut suppress reg_write using misalign_jump alone. Retain decoded\nbranch reg_write=0 and the existing next_reg_write expression. Keep\nall targets, traps, redirects, predictor training, registers and holds.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_decoder.py','description':'''Preserve all legal/reserved decoding tests and explicitly check the\ninstruction-class property used by the optimization: all six legal\nbranch functions set is_branch and clear reg_write; reserved branch\nfunctions retain illegal, nonwriting default controls.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every assertion and cycle check. Add forwarded branch and\njump misalignment cases, branch immediate bits aliasing a younger\nsource tag, trap-suppressed link-register consumers, same-rd priority\nand memory holds. Compare exact RVFI traps, operands, writes, next\nPCs, retirement order and timing against the independent reference.\n'''}]\n}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,data): return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',data,style='|' if '\\\\n' in data else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r10s0.yaml')\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final control-cone hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
