{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_37", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r11s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r11s0',\n'title':'Two radix-8 digits in the divider first recurrence',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.44 iter/sec at 73.790 MHz with 4,230,003\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Recent experiments repeatedly expose the\nfirst divider recurrence from divisor_q to remainder_bank[1]. This\nphase consumes six bits through three dependent radix-4 subtract/select\nsteps; later phases consume four bits through only two steps. Prior\nlaunch-side 3D registration gained only 0.73 percent and a three-plus-five\nbit repartition gained only 0.59 percent. Reduce the number of serial\ndigit decisions inside the existing first-phase boundary instead.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only phase p=0 of the real div_unit arithmetic with two\nradix-8 digit steps, each consuming three dividend bits. Preserve the\ntwo-bit launch, all seven successor-bank register boundaries, the\n2+6+4+4+4+4+4+4 consumed-bit partition, final sign/transfer cycle and\nnine-cycle EX occupancy. This is a combinational arithmetic micro-\noptimization, with no new pipeline stage, state or scheduling change.\n\nFor the first phase, use 11-bit unsigned trial/remainder and divisor\nmultiples, with explicitly widened 12-bit unsigned trial subtractions.\nLet D be zero-extended divisor_q[7:0]. Prepare exact D through 7D once\nbefore the two digit steps: 2D and 4D are shifts, 3D=D+2D, 5D=D+4D,\n6D=3D<<1 and 7D=(D<<3)-D. Eleven bits hold every multiple for D<=255.\nKeep the original |divisor_q[31:8] bypass of the entire phase: for\nlarger divisors, emit quotient_bank[0]<<6 and the appended dividend\nprefix as remainder. Truncated low-byte multiples must never affect\narchitectural state when that bypass is selected.\n\nInitialize Q=quotient_bank[0] and R={9'b0,remainder_bank[0][1:0]}.\nEach radix-8 digit forms T={R[7:0],Q[31:29]}. In parallel, compute\nB[k]={1'b0,T}-{1'b0,kD} for k=1..7. Bit 11 is the underflow flag b[k].\nUse exclusive selection enables take[7]=\"'!b[7], take[k]=b[k+1]&&!b[k]\nfor k=1..6, and take[0]=b[1]. Select the corresponding low 11-bit\ndifference, or T for digit zero, with a parallel masked OR. Append\nthree quotient bits { !b[4], ((!b[2]&&b[4])||!b[6]),\n(take[1]||take[3]||take[5]||take[7]) }. Repeat twice and register the\nresult in the original bank[1] on the original iteration-zero edge.\nUse explicitly sized unsigned shifts, additions and subtractions.\n\nFor D=0 all differences equal T, take[7] alone is set, and both\nquotient digits become seven while remainder retains the prefix.\nKeep the existing final division-by-zero quotient override and all\nsigned magnitude/sign correction behavior, including INT_MIN/-1 and\nremainder sign. The phase still produces exactly the same Q/R state\nas the existing three radix-4 digits for every reachable launch state.\nDo not use /, %, a runtime lookup memory or additional DSP hardware.\n\nKeep phases p=1..6 bit-for-bit unchanged, including their prefix-sized\nradix-4 arithmetic and registered full 34-bit triple_divisor_q. Continue\npreparing that full triple alongside phase zero; do not move it onto\nlaunch or feed later phases from the low-byte multiples. Keep all\nregister enables, reset values, busy/done/accept, blocked completion,\nignored starts while busy, captured operands/metadata and ALTOPS formulas\nand latency unchanged. No ordinary ALU, forwarding, predictor, memory\nbus, decoder, nret=1 IO or RVFI behavior changes are included.\n\nThis trades fourteen parallel trial subtractors and wider selection\nfor two serial decisions instead of three on the first-phase critical\npath. Multiple-generation fanout, the seven-way selection, or unchanged\nforwarded ALU/branch paths may negate the gain. The eight-percent\nforecast is provisional, not a demonstrated timing result. Require all\nthree Gowin placement options and inspect whether the first recurrence\nactually becomes shorter. At unchanged 4,230,003 bracketed CoreMark\ncycles, acceptance requires fitness strictly above 182.46424 iter/sec,\napproximately 77.183 MHz median Fmax.\n\nPreserve all existing checks. Exhaustively compare first-phase Q/R\nagainst an independent unsigned prefix-division reference for every\neight-bit dividend prefix and D=0..255. For nonzero D, check that the\nlow six quotient bits appended after the two-bit launch are correct;\nfor D=0 use the restoring all-ones quotient convention. Check large\ndivisors with low-byte aliases, signed negative operands, INT_MIN,\nall eight quotient digits and exact kD-1/kD/kD+1 decision boundaries.\nRetain per-bank prefix assertions, exact nine-cycle protocol checks,\noperand mutation, completion backpressure, reset and consecutive\nrequests. Run real and ALTOPS divider/pipeline suites, standard formal,\nRVFI cosimulation and canonical stalled CoreMark with every CRC, UART,\nbounds and marker check. Real-M formal-deep remains separate from the\nALTOPS gate and must not be represented as proved by it.\n'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'''Specialize only p=0 to two unsigned radix-8 digits with exact low-byte\nD..7D multiples, parallel 12-bit borrow-producing subtractions and\nexclusive masked selection. Preserve the whole-phase large-divisor\nbypass, seven existing banks, later radix-4 phases, full-width 3D\npreparation and identical real/ALTOPS scheduling and corner cases.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'''Preserve all existing arithmetic/protocol assertions and add exhaustive\n8-bit-prefix by 8-bit-divisor first-phase reference checks, radix-8\nmultiple boundaries, large-divisor low-byte aliases, signed magnitudes,\nD=0, reset, captured operands and retained completion. Keep exact\nper-bank and nine-cycle assertions in real and ALTOPS builds.\n'''}]}\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=78))\nprint('Wrote schema-valid',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_37", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r11s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r11s0',\n'title':'Two radix-8 digits in the divider first recurrence',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.44 iter/sec at 73.790 MHz with 4,230,003\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Recent experiments repeatedly expose the\nfirst divider recurrence from divisor_q to remainder_bank[1]. This\nphase consumes six bits through three dependent radix-4 subtract/select\nsteps; later phases consume four bits through only two steps. Prior\nlaunch-side 3D registration gained only 0.73 percent and a three-plus-five\nbit repartition gained only 0.59 percent. Reduce the number of serial\ndigit decisions inside the existing first-phase boundary instead.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace only phase p=0 of the real div_unit arithmetic with two\nradix-8 digit steps, each consuming three dividend bits. Preserve the\ntwo-bit launch, all seven successor-bank register boundaries, the\n2+6+4+4+4+4+4+4 consumed-bit partition, final sign/transfer cycle and\nnine-cycle EX occupancy. This is a combinational arithmetic micro-\noptimization, with no new pipeline stage, state or scheduling change.\n\nFor the first phase, use 11-bit unsigned trial/remainder and divisor\nmultiples, with explicitly widened 12-bit unsigned trial subtractions.\nLet D be zero-extended divisor_q[7:0]. Prepare exact D through 7D once\nbefore the two digit steps: 2D and 4D are shifts, 3D=D+2D, 5D=D+4D,\n6D=3D<<1 and 7D=(D<<3)-D. Eleven bits hold every multiple for D<=255.\nKeep the original |divisor_q[31:8] bypass of the entire phase: for\nlarger divisors, emit quotient_bank[0]<<6 and the appended dividend\nprefix as remainder. Truncated low-byte multiples must never affect\narchitectural state when that bypass is selected