t-percent\nforecast is provisional, not a demonstrated timing result. Require all\nthree Gowin placement options and inspect whether the first recurrence\nactually becomes shorter. At unchanged 4,230,003 bracketed CoreMark\ncycles, acceptance requires fitness strictly above 182.46424 iter/sec,\napproximately 77.183 MHz median Fmax.\n\nPreserve all existing checks. Exhaustively compare first-phase Q/R\nagainst an independent unsigned prefix-division reference for every\neight-bit dividend prefix and D=0..255. For nonzero D, check that the\nlow six quotient bits appended after the two-bit launch are correct;\nfor D=0 use the restoring all-ones quotient convention. Check large\ndivisors with low-byte aliases, signed negative operands, INT_MIN,\nall eight quotient digits and exact kD-1/kD/kD+1 decision boundaries.\nRetain per-bank prefix assertions, exact nine-cycle protocol checks,\noperand mutation, completion backpressure, reset and consecutive\nrequests. Run real and ALTOPS divider/pipeline suites, standard formal,\nRVFI cosimulation and canonical stalled CoreMark with every CRC, UART,\nbounds and marker check. Real-M formal-deep remains separate from the\nALTOPS gate and must not be represented as proved by it.\n'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'''Specialize only p=0 to two unsigned radix-8 digits with exact low-byte\nD..7D multiples, parallel 12-bit borrow-producing subtractions and\nexclusive masked selection. Preserve the whole-phase large-divisor\nbypass, seven existing banks, later radix-4 phases, full-width 3D\npreparation and identical real/ALTOPS scheduling and corner cases.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'''Preserve all existing arithmetic/protocol assertions and add exhaustive\n8-bit-prefix by 8-bit-divisor first-phase reference checks, radix-8\nmultiple boundaries, large-divisor low-byte aliases, signed magnitudes,\nD=0, reset, captured operands and retained completion. Keep exact\nper-bank and nine-cycle assertions in real and ALTOPS builds.\n'''}]}\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=78))\nprint('Wrote schema-valid',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Wrote schema-valid cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r11s0.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
