{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_63", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r11s0.yaml')\nd={'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r11s0','title':'Remove result-selection muxes from forwarded memory addressing','category':'micro_opt','motivation':'''The champion scores 174.44 iter/sec at 73.790 MHz and 4,230,003\nbracketed CoreMark cycles. Recent critical paths start at retained\nMEM/WB load data, pass through WB selection and forwarded EX arithmetic,\nand terminate at data memory. The prior r7s0 dedicated-address experiment\ngained 7.01 percent against the pre-multiplier-pipeline champion but was\noutscored by the multiplier retiming. The current champion still routes\naddresses through the general ALU result. Optimize this one forwarded\naddress cone at both existing register boundaries, removing result-type\nselection before and after effective-address addition.\n''','hypothesis':'''Preselect final writeback data at the existing MEM/WB input, and give\nload/store effective addresses a dedicated EX/MEM register fed directly\nby fully forwarded rs1 plus the decoded immediate. These are coordinated\nmux-placement changes along the same WB-to-EX-to-memory address cone.\nAdd no stage, request buffer, execution cycle or new interlock.\n\nReplace only mem_wb_t's separate alu_result and read_data payloads with\none 32-bit writeback_data field. In MEM, select extended load_data if\nin.ctrl.mem_to_reg, otherwise multiply_result if is_multiply, otherwise\nin.alu_result. Use three exclusive enables and a masked OR before the\nregister: load_sel=mem_to_reg, mul_sel=\"'!load_sel&&is_multiply,\nalu_sel=!load_sel&&!is_multiply. Capture the final value with the original\nMEM/WB enable. wb_stage drives w_data directly from writeback_data,\nwithout a validity, reg_write, rd or result-type mux. Keep architectural\nw_en=ctrl.reg_write&&valid and w_addr=rd. Real/ALTOPS multiply selection,\nraw RVFI memory data and all source/PC metadata remain unchanged.\n\nAdd a 32-bit effective_addr field to ex_mem_t. On each ordinary valid\nEX advance, capture rs1+in.imm directly, using the existing fully\nforwarded raw rs1 and 32-bit modular addition. Keep the general\nalu_result, partial products and write_data unchanged. The address must\nnot depend on ALU opcode/result selection, jump-link selection or the\ndivider completion-result mux. In MEM use effective_addr for dmem_addr,\nbyte masks, alignment checks, load-extraction offsets and aligned RVFI\nmemory address. Preserve all 32 address bits, including both byte-offset\nbits. For an active load/store, this value equals the old ALU_ADD result.\nAn inactive memory address bus may differ, without issuing a request.\n\nUse the original reset, valid, stall and completion priorities for both\nbundles. EX/MEM effective_addr holds through dmem backpressure and is\ncleared with the existing whole-bundle bubbles and divider metadata.\nMEM/WB hold_wb must clear only valid, retaining writeback_data and all\nmetadata even after the old instruction retires. Otherwise capture data\nalso for invalid slots, matching the previous WB mux'\"'s behavior. Never\ngate forwarding data with current WB valid or architectural write enable.\nThe same wb_w_data bus continues to serve EX, register-file write-first\nbypass and RVFI destination data. Preserve saved source-mask priority,\nx0 semantics, prospective write qualification, load/multiply-use bubbles,\ncaptured division operands, all trap suppression and exact RVFI ordering.\n\nThis targets one combinational path: registered final WB value through\nexisting one-hot rs1 forwarding and a dedicated address adder into the\naddress register. Moving load selection before MEM/WB removes its late\nmux; bypassing general execution-result selection removes the mux after\naddress arithmetic. Consolidating two WB data registers offsets the new\n32-bit address register. The costs are earlier selection on the MEM\nload/multiply inputs and possible changes in adder sharing and routing.\nThe unchanged divider and branch-recovery paths may cap the gain.\n\nThe initial eight-percent forecast is unmeasured for the combined\ncircuit. At unchanged 4,230,003 CoreMark cycles, acceptance requires\nfitness strictly above 182.46424 iter/sec, approximately 77.183 MHz median\nGowin Fmax. Require all three placement options and canonical stalled\nCoreMark with exact CRCs, UART validation, bounds and timing brackets.\nKeep nret=1 IO, decoder legality, progress and every correctness gate.\n\nRetain existing tests and cover forwarded load/store base addresses,\npositive/negative offsets, wraparound arithmetic without issuing OOB\nrequests, byte lanes, half/word alignment traps, both operand sources,\nsame-rd priority and x0. Exercise ordinary ALU, load, jump-link, all four\nmultiply variants and completed DIV/REM values through WB and register-\nfile bypass, in real and ALTOPS builds. Stress retained invalid WB data\nwhile an intervening memory request stalls and a younger instruction\nuses that value as its address base. Check exact RVFI source/result and\nmemory fields, stable stalled requests, retirement order and unchanged\ninstruction timing. Run unchanged standard formal, real arithmetic tests,\nRVFI cosimulation and vendor timing; do not relax existing assertions.\n''','expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add ex_mem_t.effective_addr and consolidate only mem_wb_t alu_result/read_data into writeback_data; preserve other pipeline and RVFI fields.'},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Register fully forwarded rs1+imm directly as effective_addr on ordinary valid EX advance, retaining existing whole-bundle reset, hold, bubble and divider-completion handling.'},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'Use effective_addr consistently for every memory address/offset/alignment consumer. Preselect load/multiply/ordinary writeback value before MEM/WB using exclusive enables; preserve held data, trap qualification, raw memory reporting and ALTOPS behavior.'},\n{'file':'rtl/wb_stage.sv','description':'Drive w_data directly from registered writeback_data, preserving w_en, w_addr and invalid-but-retained forwarding values.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve all tests and add active memory-address equivalence, forwarded base/offset, byte-lane, alignment-trap, retained-WB and mixed result-type sequences, checking real/ALTOPS RVFI values and exact cycles.'}]}\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=78))\nprint('Wrote schema-valid',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
