new\n32-bit address register. The costs are earlier selection on the MEM\nload/multiply inputs and possible changes in adder sharing and routing.\nThe unchanged divider and branch-recovery paths may cap the gain.\n\nThe initial eight-percent forecast is unmeasured for the combined\ncircuit. At unchanged 4,230,003 CoreMark cycles, acceptance requires\nfitness strictly above 182.46424 iter/sec, approximately 77.183 MHz median\nGowin Fmax. Require all three placement options and canonical stalled\nCoreMark with exact CRCs, UART validation, bounds and timing brackets.\nKeep nret=1 IO, decoder legality, progress and every correctness gate.\n\nRetain existing tests and cover forwarded load/store base addresses,\npositive/negative offsets, wraparound arithmetic without issuing OOB\nrequests, byte lanes, half/word alignment traps, both operand sources,\nsame-rd priority and x0. Exercise ordinary ALU, load, jump-link, all four\nmultiply variants and completed DIV/REM values through WB and register-\nfile bypass, in real and ALTOPS builds. Stress retained invalid WB data\nwhile an intervening memory request stalls and a younger instruction\nuses that value as its address base. Check exact RVFI source/result and\nmemory fields, stable stalled requests, retirement order and unchanged\ninstruction timing. Run unchanged standard formal, real arithmetic tests,\nRVFI cosimulation and vendor timing; do not relax existing assertions.\n''','expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add ex_mem_t.effective_addr and consolidate only mem_wb_t alu_result/read_data into writeback_data; preserve other pipeline and RVFI fields.'},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Register fully forwarded rs1+imm directly as effective_addr on ordinary valid EX advance, retaining existing whole-bundle reset, hold, bubble and divider-completion handling.'},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'Use effective_addr consistently for every memory address/offset/alignment consumer. Preselect load/multiply/ordinary writeback value before MEM/WB using exclusive enables; preserve held data, trap qualification, raw memory reporting and ALTOPS behavior.'},\n{'file':'rtl/wb_stage.sv','description':'Drive w_data directly from registered writeback_data, preserving w_en, w_addr and invalid-but-retained forwarding values.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Preserve all tests and add active memory-address equivalence, forwarded base/offset, byte-lane, alignment-trap, retained-WB and mixed result-type sequences, checking real/ALTOPS RVFI values and exact cycles.'}]}\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=78))\nprint('Wrote schema-valid',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
