{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r11s0.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nold='''The initial eight-percent forecast is unmeasured for the combined\ncircuit. At unchanged 4,230,003 CoreMark cycles, acceptance requires\nfitness strictly above 182.46424 iter/sec, approximately 77.183 MHz median\nGowin Fmax. Require all three placement options and canonical stalled\nCoreMark with exact CRCs, UART validation, bounds and timing brackets.\nKeep nret=1 IO, decoder legality, progress and every correctness gate.\n'''\nnew='''An isolated prototype of exactly this combined cone change measured\nGowin placement options 0/1/2 at 70.677, 75.082 and 75.082 MHz: median\n75.082 MHz. Option zero used 5,427 LUT4s and 1,213 registers, versus the\nchampion's 5,422 and 1,214; LUT RAM, BSRAM and DSP counts were unchanged.\nThe worst reported path moved to existing branch/predictor-training\nlogic. The individual writeback and dedicated-address variants reached\n73.136 and 71.284 MHz median respectively, supporting evaluation of the\ncomplete forwarded-address cone rather than either local mux alone.\n\nAt unchanged 4,230,003 CoreMark cycles, the combined result implies\n177.4966 iter/sec, 1.75 percent above 174.44. This does NOT meet the\nrequired 4.6-percent acceptance margin. Forecast two percent with medium\nconfidence, reflecting the measured candidate rather than an unsupported\neight-percent claim. Acceptance still requires fitness strictly above\n182.46424 iter/sec, approximately 77.183 MHz at those cycles. Reproduce\nall three placement options and canonical stalled CoreMark with exact\nCRCs, UART validation, bounds and timing brackets. Retain the champion\nunless the unchanged threshold is exceeded. Keep nret=1 IO, decoder\nlegality, progress and every correctness gate.\n'''\nasse