{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"agent_message","text":"I found a narrower way to test the control issue: give the load/store address register its own capture enable. Earlier address-separation attempts still cleared or selected that register during bubbles and divider completion. This version uses only reset and data-memory stall for its enable, while preserving the existing request and trap checks.\n"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_54", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r15s0.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261001-001-r15s0\ntitle: \\\"Isolate effective-address capture from EX bubble and divider controls\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 174.44 iterations/sec at 73.790 MHz and 4,230,003\n  bracketed CoreMark cycles. Repeated vendor paths run from retained WB\n  data through EX arithmetic to the data-memory address input. The r7s0\n  dedicated-address experiment improved the earlier champion, but r11s0\n  combined address/writeback changes gained only 1.75 percent on this\n  champion. Those address registers still participated in whole-EX/MEM\n  bubble clearing and divider-result selection. Remove those unnecessary\n  control dependencies from this one timed address datapath.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give the existing load/store effective-address calculation a dedicated\n  32-bit register whose only controls are reset and the existing EX/MEM\n  data-memory stall. Compute fully forwarded raw rs1 plus the decoded\n  immediate directly, with modulo-2\"'^32 addition. Capture that sum on every\n  non-reset, non-stalled edge, including invalid EX slots and division\n  execution/completion. This is a local register-enable and mux-placement\n  micro-optimization; add no pipeline stage, instruction cycle or interlock.\n\n  Add effective_addr to ex_mem_t for transport into MEM. Keep the storage\n  separate from the whole-bundle reg_q assignments in ex_stage: declare\n  effective_addr_q, reset it to zero, otherwise update it only when !stall.\n  Construct out from the original reg_q and override out.effective_addr\n  with effective_addr_q in one combinational assignment block. No storage\n  bit may have multiple procedural drivers. The redundant reg_q address\n  field is unused and can be pruned. Alternatively split the payload type\n  cleanly, but the address storage must retain the exact independent enable.\n\n  Do not clear or hold effective_addr_q for !in.valid, execute_busy,\n  div_done, redirects, prediction mismatch, trap state or ALU opcode. Do not\n  route it through the ALU-result mux, PC+4 link selection, division-result\n  mux or zero-bubble mux. Retain all 32 address bits and use the existing\n  raw rs1 forwarding network, whose saved masks include retained invalid\n  MEM/WB data. Do not add current WB-valid or write-enable qualifications.\n\n  In mem_stage use in.effective_addr for dmem_addr, byte-mask offsets,\n  half/word alignment checks, load-data extraction offsets and the aligned\n  RVFI memory address. Keep in.alu_result for ordinary result writeback and\n  multiply selection. Keep every original valid-qualified memory enable,\n  alignment trap and suppressed write. An inactive address bus may differ;\n  every active request and accepted RVFI memory access must be identical.\n  During dmem backpressure the address register holds alongside EX/MEM,\n  guaranteeing a stable request until acceptance. DIV/REM never issue a\n  memory request, so their arbitrary captured address is unobservable.\n\n  Preserve the original EX/MEM whole-bundle reset/bubble/divider behavior\n  for all other fields, all ID payload holds, and the MEM/WB retained-data\n  rule. Keep arithmetic and ALTOPS formulas, division scheduling, decoder\n  defaults, misalignment traps, source priority, predictor policy, nret=1\n  IO, exact-once retirement and both bus handshakes unchanged.\n\n  The intended timing cone is retained WB value through the existing raw\n  forwarding mux and one addition into a register controlled only by dmem\n  stall. The gain must come from removing real result/control muxes, not\n  changing constraints or relying on an inactive request. Cost is a new\n  32-bit address register and possible extra adder/routing resources. The\n  unchanged first divider recurrence and branch recovery may limit Fmax.\n  The six-percent estimate is speculative pending vendor measurement.\n\n  Preserve all existing tests and exact-cycle assertions. Exercise load\n  and store bases forwarded from each producer, x0, same-rd writer priority,\n  load/multiply dependency bubbles, and completed DIV/REM results. Include\n  prolonged data stalls retaining an invalid WB producer, simultaneous\n  instruction stalls, wrong-path memory instructions, all byte lanes,\n  negative offsets, carry propagation and alignment traps. Test modular\n  address arithmetic without issuing out-of-bounds transactions. Check\n  stability of active stalled requests, exact RVFI memory/source/result\n  fields, trap suppression, next PCs and ordered retirement. Run unchanged\n  standard formal, RVFI cosimulation and the canonical CoreMark CRC, UART,\n  bounds and timing-marker checks; do not weaken any assertions.\n\n  With identical scheduling, expect 4,230,003 bracketed CoreMark cycles for\n  the same stall sequence. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above\n  182.46424 iterations/sec, approximately 77.184 MHz median Gowin Fmax at\n  that cycle count. Measure all three placement options and retain the\n  champion unless the greater-than-4.6-percent margin is observed.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a full-width effective_addr transport field to ex_mem_t without\n      changing any top-level ports, stage boundary or retirement width.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Add separate effective_addr_q storage for fully forwarded rs1+imm,\n      reset to zero and enabled solely by !stall. Override the output bundle'\"'s\n      address field with this register; retain all existing assignments and\n      priorities for the original EX/MEM payload, bubbles and divider result.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Use effective_addr consistently for physical and RVFI memory addressing,\n      byte lanes, load extraction and alignment checks. Preserve all memory\n      enable/trap qualifications and ordinary ALU/multiply writeback data.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve existing assertions and instruction timing. Add active-address\n      stability and RVFI checks spanning bubbles, division completion, each\n      forwarded base source, retained WB data, both bus stalls, byte lanes,\n      negative offsets, carry boundaries and misaligned access suppression.\n''')\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated hypothesis; schema validation passed.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
