ycle unchanged.\n\n  In reg_file.sv, retain the existing 32x32 array, synchronous writes,\n  complete reset-to-zero behavior, asynchronous reads, x0 semantics and\n  same-cycle write-first bypass. Add the Gowin-supported declaration\n  attribute (* syn_ramstyle = \\\"distributed_ram\\\" *) to that array. Do not\n  replace reset with uninitialized storage or change register-file latency.\n  The prototype maps the complete core to 40 LUT-RAMs and four BSRAMs,\n  compared with eight LUT-RAMs and six BSRAMs for the champion. This is a\n  physical storage implementation change; portable simulation and formal\n  retain the same register-file behavior.\n\n  Compute forwarding decisions for the instruction currently in decode,\n  using raw imem_data[19:15] and [24:20]. Compare each source with the\n  destination of the instruction currently in ID/EX, which will occupy\n  EX/MEM after an accepted decode edge, and with the destination currently\n  in EX/MEM, which will occupy MEM/WB after that edge. These are prospective\n  producer tags, not the current-stage tags used by the old EX comparator.\n\n  Export next_reg_write from EX as in.valid && ctrl_with_trap.reg_write,\n  using the existing resolved misalignment suppression. Export the\n  prospective MEM/WB write flag from MEM as ctrl_with_trap.reg_write,\n  including memory-alignment suppression. Use these flags to qualify the\n  two prospective producer matches, always excluding destination x0.\n  EX/MEM remains the younger producer and has priority over MEM/WB.\n  For each source encode bit 1 = matching younger producer, bit 2 =\n  matching older producer AND NOT bit 1, and bit 0 = neither producer.\n  Exactly one source enable is set for every accepted decode instruction.\n  Preserve the existing qualification semantics rather than using WB's\n  valid-gated architectural write enable as a forwarding qualification.\n\n  Add two three-bit raw source masks and two four-bit ALU source masks\n  to id_ex_t. Capture them with the existing \"'!stall payload enable in\n  id_stage, reset them deterministically, and hold them whenever the\n  corresponding instruction payload is held. As with the current payload,\n  flush controls validity and prediction metadata, not these source masks.\n  Form alu_a_sel = {dec_is_auipc, raw_rs1_mask & {3{!dec_is_auipc}}}\n  and alu_b_sel = {dec_alu_src, raw_rs2_mask & {3{!dec_alu_src}}}\n  before the ID/EX edge. The high bit selects PC or immediate; lower bits\n  retain the raw source ordering. Legal decode and default-illegal behavior\n  remain unchanged.\n\n  In EX, each raw operand is the OR of the three original data sources\n  masked by its registered raw enables: in.rsN_val, fwd_ex_mem and\n  fwd_mem_wb. Independently form alu_a and alu_b from those original\n  sources and PC/immediate using the registered four-bit masks. Avoid\n  recreating a forwarding mux followed by an ALU-source mux. Keep raw\n  forwarded operands available for branches, JALR, stores, divider capture\n  and RVFI even when the ALU selects PC or immediate. Preserve the original\n  ALU, multiplier, divider arithmetic and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas.\n\n  The key scheduling condition is that source masks are only consumed by\n  the instruction with which they were captured. During dmem holds, ID/EX\n  and EX/MEM remain fixed and MEM/WB retains forwarding data despite valid\n  clearing, so the saved choices remain correct. During division, capture\n  operands and metadata once with the existing div_start; later held masks\n  need not reselect drained producers because the divider uses its captured\n  operands. On division completion, the held ID/EX destination becomes the\n  prospective EX/MEM producer for the newly accepted younger instruction.\n  Load-use bubbles, redirects, invalid slots and reset must not introduce\n  stale-mask execution. Trap-suppressed writes must never win a match.\n  Check these conditions with existing assertions and formal, not new\n  assumptions that restrict legal instruction or stall streams.\n\n  The prototype changes only this operand-read and source-control cone.\n  Option-0 area is 3,404 LUT4s, 702 registers, 40 LUT-RAMs, four BSRAMs\n  and six DSPs, versus 3,277 LUT4s, 739 registers, eight LUT-RAMs, six\n  BSRAMs and six DSPs for the champion. The timing flow uses the unchanged\n  FPGA wrapper, stall generator, constraints and all three placement\n  options. At unchanged 4,194,434 CoreMark cycles, 59.313 MHz predicts\n  about 141.41 iterations/second, 15.45 percent above 122.48. Acceptance\n  requires fitness strictly above 128.11408, approximately 53.737 MHz.\n  Forecast 15 percent with medium confidence; mapping sensitivity and\n  incorrect prospective-producer qualification remain the main risks.\n\n  Early-selection RTL passed the existing pipeline suite, five-program\n  architectural/CRC cosimulation, and canonical stalled CoreMark with\n  exactly 4,194,434 bracketed cycles, no OOB, all five canonical CRCs and\n  the required validation text. Distributed-RAM mapping changes no RTL\n  semantics. Re-run correctness and vendor timing for the final combined\n  implementation; preliminary measurements are not an accepted eval.\n  Preserve nret=1, exact core IO, strict RVFI ordering, all trap checks,\n  bounded progress, nine-cycle division occupancy and every eval contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 15\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: |\n      Request distributed RAM for the existing register array with\n      syn_ramstyle = \"distributed_ram\". Preserve all reset, read, write,\n      x0 and write-first behavior; confirm the two register-file BSRAMs\n      disappear in Gowin'\"'s mapped netlist.\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Produce three mutually exclusive source enables per decoded source.\n      Preserve younger-producer priority and x0 exclusion. The core now\n      supplies decode source tags and prospective EX/MEM and MEM/WB\n      producer tags and trap-qualified write flags.\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Extend id_ex_t with raw rs1/rs2 source masks of three bits each and\n      complete ALU A/B source masks of four bits each. No new pipeline\n      boundary, retirement channel or arithmetic state is needed.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Accept prospective forwarding masks, combine them with this\n      instruction's decoded AUIPC/immediate controls, and capture all\n      four masks with the existing payload enable. Reset masks, hold\n      with payload, and preserve validity-only flush semantics.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Export the prospective EX/MEM producer's valid, trap-qualified\n      register-write flag. Select raw and ALU operands with registered\n      masks and parallel masked-OR logic. Preserve every raw operand\n      consumer, divider capture/completion and existing EX/MEM update.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Export the prospective MEM/WB register-write flag from the existing\n      ctrl_with_trap, preserving alignment suppression and all bus,\n      load-data, retained-forwarding and retirement behavior.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Rewire forwarding comparisons to raw decode source tags, current\n      ID/EX and EX/MEM destination tags, and the new prospective producer\n      flags. Feed masks into ID and registered raw masks into EX. Preserve\n      hazard logic, current forwarding data buses and external nret=1 IO.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every existing test. Add independent youngest-writer checks\n      for the saved masks and cycle-stamped RVFI/results across simultaneous\n      producer matches, x0, AUIPC/immediate overrides, both raw operands,\n      load-use bubbles, dmem holds with invalid-but-retained WB data,\n      division launch/completion and an immediately dependent consumer,\n      redirect squashes, reset, and misaligned loads or jumps that suppress\n      destination writes. Verify unchanged retirement and memory cycles\n      under deterministic stall schedules.\n''')\nimport json, yaml, jsonschema\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(h,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert h['id']=='hyp-20261001-001-r5s0' and h['category']=='micro_opt'\nprint('Schema valid:',p)\nprint('Predicted fitness:',59.313*1e7/4194434)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Schema valid: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r5s0.yaml\nPredicted fitness: 141.40882893854092\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
