timing limiting the new clock.\n  Judge the unchanged three-option Gowin median times measured\n  iterations/cycle, not the disappearance of a single critical path.\n\n  Validate load/store addresses and RVFI byte lanes for all access\n  widths, sign extensions and alignment faults; forwarded bases from\n  ALU, loads, MUL and completed DIV; positive/negative offsets and\n  32-bit wraparound in unit tests; same-rd producer priority; and\n  multi-cycle memory stalls. Compare request addresses only while a\n  load/store request is active and preserve exact instruction and\n  memory-acceptance cycles. Run existing pipeline and RVFI cosim\n  gates, standard formal, then stalled CoreMark with all canonical\n  CRCs, validation text, memory bounds and timing markers intact.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 10\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a 32-bit effective_addr field to ex_mem_t, distinct from the\n      general alu_result and from the RVFI-only aligned memory address.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture fully forwarded rs1 plus the decoded immediate directly\n      into effective_addr at the existing EX/MEM boundary. Hold, reset\n      and clear it with its instruction. Preserve general ALU result,\n      jump/link, divider completion, metadata and forwarding behavior.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive dmem_addr and all address-dependent byte-lane, alignment,\n      load extraction and RVFI memory-address logic from effective_addr.\n      Keep the general alu_result transfer into MEM/WB unchanged, along\n      with memory enables, store data, traps, load extension and holds.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain existing assertions and add directed load/store address\n      checks with ALU/load/MUL/DIV-forwarded bases, all byte/half/word\n      lanes, negative offsets and alignment traps. Exercise dmem holds,\n      simultane