nProvide divisor_bank[0:6] and full 34-bit triple_bank[1:6]. Each phase\np reads only divisor_bank[p], and phases 1..6 read triple_bank[p]. On\nthe existing phase-p enabled edge, copy D into divisor_bank[p+1] when\np<6. On the phase-zero edge compute full 34-bit 3D from divisor_bank[0]\nand capture it in triple_bank[1], in parallel with the first recurrence.\nFor p=1..5, copy triple_bank[p] into triple_bank[p+1] on the same edge\nthat advances its quotient/remainder successor. There is no indexed\noperand-bank read mux and no extra clock boundary or divider iteration.\nUse the local D for each phase's large-divisor predicate and d1/d2.\nKeep every width, borrow test, mutually exclusive digit-selection mask,\nquotient/remainder bank and sign-correction result unchanged.\n\nReset all new registers to zero and use the exact existing advancement\ncondition active_q && \"'!complete_q && iteration_q==p for phase copies.\nCapture bank zero and the narrow triple only on start && !busy. Preserve\nresult retention when accept is low, reset cancellation, ignored starts\nwhile busy, divide-by-zero quotient/remainder, signed INT_MIN/-1, and\nexactly one completion acceptance. Do not change the ALTOPS formulas or\nreal/ALTOPS scheduling, EX control, forwarding, memory stalls or nret=1.\nAll newly introduced arithmetic belongs inside the real-arithmetic\nbranch; the ALTOPS timing controller remains identical.\n\nThis removes preparation arithmetic from the first recurrence and\nreduces divisor operand broadcast fanout and routing across physically\nseparate banks. It costs additional operand registers and clock load.\nThe narrow-triple-only prototype measured 74.330 MHz median versus\n73.790 MHz, below the 4.6 percent acceptance margin; that partial change\nalone is insufficient. Phase-local storage is intended to extend the\nbenefit, but its forecast remains unmeasured until the complete prototype\nfinishes. Other EX/ALU paths and added registers may limit the result.\nCoreMark should retain exactly 4,230,003 bracketed cycles. Acceptance\nrequires fitness above 182.46424, approximately 77.185 MHz at that count.\n\nRetain all existing real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU reference tests and add phase\nboundary checks for D around 4,16,64,256, each later prefix power of two,\nunsigned high-bit values, signed extrema and zero. Check quotient and\nremainder against an independent integer oracle, including all signs,\nback-to-back starts, reset and prolonged accept=0. Verify no operand bank\nis consumed before its enabled predecessor copy. Run unchanged pipeline,\ncosimulation and formal gates; default ALTOPS formal is not evidence of\nreal division arithmetic correctness. Preserve all canonical CoreMark\nCRCs, UART text, bounds and marker timing checks, and measure median\nGowin Fmax across the evaluator'\"'s three placement options.\n'''\nx['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'}\nx['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'''Precompute the exact narrow first-phase triple at launch, and replace\nglobal D/3D broadcasts with statically consumed operand banks copied\non the existing phase-enable edges. Preserve all recurrence values,\nbypasses, result behavior, handshake schedule and ALTOPS timing.\n'''},{'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'''Keep all exact RV32M comparisons and add divisor-prefix boundary,\nphase-local operand progression, reset, back-to-back request and held\ncompletion coverage for signed and unsigned division and remainder.\n'''}]\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef rep(d,s): return d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,rep)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(x,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False))\njsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and schema-validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Updated and schema-validated cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r8s0.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
