{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_106", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r8s0.yaml')\nx=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nx['title']='Two radix-8 digits in the narrow first divider recurrence'\nx['motivation']='''The champion scores 174.44 at 73.790 MHz and 4,230,003 bracketed\nCoreMark cycles. Fresh Gowin timing reproduces its 71.996 MHz option-zero\nresult and nearly tied forwarding, branch and divider paths. Several\nisolated local datapath prototypes moved the bottleneck back to the\nfirst divider recurrence. That phase produces six quotient bits with\nthree dependent radix-4 subtract/select steps, unlike the two steps in\nlater phases. Earlier micro_opt work showed that off-path multiple\npreparation and fewer dependent digit steps can improve Fmax without\nadding DIV/REM cycles. Restrict the higher radix to this narrow phase.\n'''\nx['hypothesis']='''Replace only the real divider's first six-bit recurrence with two\nradix-8 digits, keeping every existing register boundary and phase\nschedule. Preserve the two-bit launch, six-bit first recurrence, six\nfour-bit later recurrences and nine-cycle EX occupancy. This is a local\narithmetic implementation change, not a new divider architecture.\n\nAt the existing start && \"'!busy operand-capture edge, retain full signed\nmagnitude conversion and additionally register exact multiples of the\nunsigned low byte D8=divisor_magnitude[7:0]: 3D8 in ten bits, and 5D8 and\n7D8 in eleven bits. Compute them independently using widened D8+2D8,\nD8+4D8 and 8D8-D8; avoid a dependent multiple-generation chain. Reset\nthese registers to zero and hold them until the next accepted request.\nDo not put the full 32-bit 3D addition on this launch path.\n\nFor p=0, use eleven-bit trial/remainder arithmetic and exactly two digit\nsteps. Form each trial T={R[7:0],Q[31:29]}. Prepare exact eleven-bit\nD,2D,3D,4D,5D,6D,7D: D and shifted copies come from the captured divisor\nlow byte; 3D,5D,7D come from the launch registers; 6D is registered 3D\nshifted once. Compute all seven {1'\"'b0,T}-{1'b0,kD} in parallel as unsigned\ntwelve-bit subtractions. With borrow[k]=diff[k][11], select digit 7 with\n\"'!borrow[7], digit k=1..6 with borrow[k+1] && !borrow[k], and digit zero\nwith borrow[1]. Select the remainder through mutually exclusive masked\nORs of the seven low-eleven-bit differences and T. Append the selected\nthree-bit digit to Q[28:0]. Repeat once and register the existing bank-1\nquotient and remainder, exactly where the old three radix-4 digits end.\n\nPreserve the phase-zero large-D bypass when divisor_q[31:8] is nonzero:\nQnext=Q<<6 and Rnext=(R<<6)|(Q>>26). Such D cannot be subtracted from the\nat-most-eight-bit consumed dividend prefix, so the truncated multiples\nmust never affect the registered result. For D<256 all multiples are\nexact; the selected remainder is below D, and for D=0 each digit is 7\nwhile the dividend prefix is retained. Keep full-width 3D preparation\non the existing phase-zero edge for later phases. All p=1..6 radix-4\nrecurrences, prefix widths, large-D bypasses and operand banks stay\nunchanged. Do not generalize radix 8 to full-width later phases.\n\nKeep quotient/remainder selection and sign correction, divide-by-zero,\nINT_MIN/-1, start/busy/done/accept timing, held completion, reset\ncancellation and ignored starts unchanged. Preserve the original\nRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS arithmetic formulas and identical real/ALTOPS timing.\nLeave all EX controls, forwarding, traps, memory handshakes, predictor,\nnret=1 IO and ordered retirement intact. Preserve existing observable\nquotient_q, remainder_q, divisor_q and triple_divisor_q values used by\nunit checks at every phase boundary.\n\nThe expected timing benefit is one fewer dependent subtract/select\nstep in the narrow first recurrence, with divisor multiples available\nbefore the phase begins. Later full-width phases keep radix 4 to avoid\nseven large subtractors per digit. Costs are roughly thirty additional\nmultiple-register bits, wider first-phase digit selection and additional\nnarrow trial subtractors. Operand capture or a non-divider path may\nbecome limiting. A narrow-3D-only trial reached 74.330 MHz median, only\n0.73 percent above 73.790 MHz and below the acceptance margin; the\nsix-bit radix change is intended to provide the additional depth cut.\nCoreMark cycles should stay exactly 4,230,003. The forecast is provisional\nuntil the full prototype is measured; acceptance requires fitness above\n182.46424, approximately 77.185 MHz at that cycle count.\n\nRetain all existing DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU tests and check exact intermediate\nquotient/remainder values after every existing edge. Add independent\ninteger-oracle coverage for all first-phase prefixes and D=0..255,\nlarge-divisor bypass boundaries, radix-8 digits 0..7, multiples kD plus\nor minus one, signed extrema and random full-width operands. Exercise\nback-to-back operations, ignored busy starts, reset and accept=0 holds.\nRun unchanged pipeline, cosimulation and formal gates; default ALTOPS\nformal does not prove real division arithmetic. Preserve canonical\nstalled CoreMark CRCs, UART validation, memory bounds and timing markers,\nand measure median Gowin Fmax across all evaluator placement options.\n'\"'''\nx['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'}\nx['changes']=[{'file':'rtl/div_unit.sv','description':'''Prepare narrow 3D/5D/7D at launch and compute the first six quotient\nbits as two radix-8 digits with parallel widened trial subtractions.\nPreserve the large-divisor bypass and every phase boundary, later\nradix-4 phase, intermediate mathematical value, handshake and ALTOPS\nschedule; retain observation aliases used by existing unit assertions.\n'''},{'file':'test/test_div_unit.py','description':'''Preserve existing arithmetic and handshake checks. Add exhaustive\nfirst-phase byte-prefix/divisor comparisons, radix-8 selection\nboundaries and large-divisor bypass cases against an independent\ninteger oracle, including signed operations and held completions.\n'''}]\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda d,s:d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(x,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False))\njsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and schema-validated hypothesis')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
