{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_118", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema,shutil\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-001-r8s0.yaml')\nx={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-001-r8s0',\n'title':'Compare branch source candidates before forwarding selection',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 174.44 at 73.790 MHz and 4,230,003 bracketed\nCoreMark cycles. A fresh Gowin option-zero run reproduces 71.996 MHz\nand the worst path from ID/EX raw_rs1_mask[2] through EX to fetch PC.\nThe detailed path traverses the forwarded operand mux, a full-width\ncomparison carry chain and redirect control. Earlier r5s0 work moved\nforwarding decisions into ID/EX, but a late high-fanout source-enable\nstill precedes branch comparison. Recent divider and multiply work has\nexposed this branch path. Local shifter, writeback and address prototypes\ndid not clear the acceptance margin, so focus on removing the source\nselection delay from the measured branch-comparison chain itself.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Move conditional-branch source selection after comparison. Compute\none-bit branch predicates for each pair of existing forwarding source\ncandidates in parallel, and select the predicate using the two saved\none-hot source masks. This is one combinational EX datapath optimization;\nkeep pipeline boundaries, instruction latency and branch recovery timing.\n\nDefine A[0]=in.rs1_val, A[1]=fwd_ex_mem, A[2]=fwd_mem_wb, and similarly\nB[0]=in.rs2_val, B[1]=fwd_ex_mem, B[2]=fwd_mem_wb. For each i,j in 0..2,\ncompute P[i,j] from the unchanged branch_op: equality for BEQ, inequality\nfor BNE, signed less-than/greater-or-equal for BLT/BGE, and unsigned\nless-than/greater-or-equal for BLTU/BGEU. Reserved branch_op values must\nretain a false predicate. Form branch_cond as a balanced reduction OR\nof P[i,j] & in.raw_rs1_mask[i] & in.raw_rs2_mask[j]. Avoid a priority mux,\na forwarding mux before these comparators, or fresh EX tag comparisons.\nA portable combinational function with the original six branch cases\nand generated source-pair instances is a concrete implementation.\n\nWhen both sources select the same shared forwarded bus, their operands\nare identical: pairs (1,1) and (2,2) can constant-fold to true for BEQ,\nBGE and BGEU and false for BNE, BLT and BLTU. Preserve these identities\nand allow ordinary synthesis sharing of opposite comparisons. Do not\nreplicate whole ALUs or target adders. Retain the existing raw rs1/rs2\nmuxes for RVFI operand capture, JALR targets, division and store data.\nThe comparator matrix must read original candidate buses directly.\n\nUse the new branch_cond in the existing branch_taken expression and\nleave branch/jump targets, actual_taken, misalignment detection,\nredirect qualification, prediction recovery and predictor training\nunchanged. All valid executing branches already have exactly one source\nselected in each registered mask; preserve that invariant, x0 and the\nyounger-producer priority. Do not qualify a candidate bus with current\nWB valid or write enable: retained invalid MEM/WB data is a required\nforwarding source during memory stalls. Invalid instruction payloads\nremain unable to redirect, train or retire. Keep the unchanged nret=1\nIO, decoder legality, load/multiply interlocks, divider schedule,\nALTOPS formulas, bus handshakes and exact retirement accounting.\n\nThis changes the late-mask path from operand mux then full comparison\nto selection of already-computed one-bit predicates. Operand data can\nbegin comparison before source selection settles. The tradeoff is more\ncomparators, candidate-bus fanout and routing; WB data arrival, unchanged\nredirect control, divider recurrence or memory arithmetic may instead\nlimit Fmax. The eight percent forecast is speculative, not a measured\ngain. The proposal adds no cycles: expect 4,230,003 bracketed CoreMark\ncycles with the same stall sequence. Acceptance requires fitness above\n182.46424, approximately 77.185 MHz at that cycle count. Evaluate with\nall three Gowin placement options and retain only a gain above 4.6 percent.\n\nRetain existing tests and exercise all nine source-pair selections for\nall six branches. Include equality, signed extrema, opposite signs,\nunsigned high bits and low-bit differences that propagate across a\ncomparison carry chain. Check both operands forwarded from the same\nproducer, same-rd older/younger priority, x0, load/multiply-use bubbles,\ncompleted division, and held WB data during prolonged dmem stalls.\nCheck actual next PC, original RVFI operands, predictor recovery and\ntraining behavior, and exact-once ordered retirement. Exercise taken\nmisaligned targets and untaken branches with misaligned immediates.\nRun unchanged standard formal and RVFI cosimulation gates and stalled\nCoreMark CRC, UART, bounds and marker checks. Do not weaken any checks.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace branch comparison after raw operand selection with parallel\nsource-pair predicates and selection by the existing registered\none-hot rs1/rs2 masks. Keep all raw operand muxes for other consumers,\nall branch-control/target logic, pipeline registers and stalls intact.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Extend directed branch tests to all source-pair and branch-function\ncombinations, signedness boundaries, same-producer comparisons,\nsame-rd priority, x0, load/multiply/divider dependencies, retained WB\nforwarding, misalignment and simultaneous bus stalls. Preserve all\nexisting assertions and check original RVFI operands and next PC.\n'''}]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\nDumper.add_representer(str,lambda d,s:d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(x,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False))\njsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nshutil.copytree('cores/bench/test','cores/bench/generated/specbranch_probe/test',dirs_exist_ok=True)\nprint('Updated and schema-validated hypothesis')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
