ad selection independent\n  of redirect/flush/validity. Use separate continuous assignments for\n  payload and validity so no artificial packed-bundle combinational\n  dependency feeds flush back into the source-index comparisons.\n\n  Let stall be the existing frontend stall output after the above\n  availability change. Outside reset/recovery, fetch_accept is\n  io_imemReady && (\"'!buffer_valid || !stall). Advance the request PC\n  only on fetch_accept, using the existing prediction computed from\n  that request PC and its actual bus instruction. If fetch_accept\n  and (buffer_valid || stall), capture the bus tuple into the buffer\n  and set buffer_valid. This covers an empty buffer accepting during\n  a backend hold and simultaneous consume/refill of an occupied\n  buffer. Otherwise, if !stall, clear buffer_valid: a buffered head\n  has drained without refill or an empty-buffer response bypassed\n  straight into decode. Otherwise retain the buffer. Never overwrite\n  a full buffer while its head is held. The buffer must support one\n  instruction per cycle under continuous ready buses.\n\n  Recovery has final priority: install redirect_target as the request\n  PC, invalidate the buffer and squash the younger ID/EX validity.\n  Discard any same-edge speculative response. Reset returns the PC\n  to zero and empties the buffer. An instruction-bus stall alone\n  must not discard a valid buffered head. A backend hold may capture\n  at most the available buffer capacity; it must not launch, retire\n  or train a buffered instruction early. Save predicted_taken when\n  the response is fetched, including simultaneous predictor training,\n  and use that saved bit when the head reaches EX. Recomputing its\n  prediction on dequeue would associate it with a different table\n  state and break direction recovery. Keep direct-target alignment\n  checks, JALR recovery and one training event per advancing branch.\n\n  Preserve exactly one ordered RVFI retirement, original instruction\n  PCs and raw operands, x0, illegal/misalignment traps, stable blocked\n  data-memory requests and exact-once stores. Preserve all multiply\n  and divider arithmetic, ALTOPS formulas, nine-cycle DIV occupancy,\n  load/multiply dependency interlocks and the frozen ready-bus\n  retirement-progress bound. Keep nret=1 and every external port.\n\n  A temporary one-entry prototype reduced canonical stalled CoreMark\n  from 4,230,003 to 4,022,833 marker-bracketed cycles, a 5.15-percent\n  improvement in iterations/cycle, with canonical CRCs, validation\n  text and no out-of-bounds accesses. Selftest and three random\n  programs each passed full RVFI cosimulation with and without both\n  bus stalls. These are preliminary measurements. The extra head mux,\n  buffer control fanout and changed placement can reduce Fmax; the\n  unchanged three-option Gowin median must determine net fitness.\n\n  Update frontend test reference models to track the independent\n  request PC and queued decode head, accepted responses, saved\n  predictions, simultaneous dequeue/refill, and recovery cancellation.\n  Existing cycle snapshots assume fetch PC equals decode PC and that\n  imemReady alone determines decode validity; replace those obsolete\n  scheduling expectations with an independent elastic-frontend model,\n  retaining full RVFI, operand, memory, arithmetic, predictor-training,\n  reset and progress assertions. Do not drop correctness coverage to\n  accommodate changed instruction-fetch timing. Test buffer empty/full,\n  downstream stalls, imem stalls during buffered issue, saved prediction\n  changes, producer priority, reset while full, recovery while full\n  and wrong-path load/store/divide cancellation.\n\n  Run unchanged formal and architectural cosim gates and the adapted\n  pipeline tests. Reproduce canonical stalled CoreMark and vendor\n  timing. Acceptance still requires fitness strictly above 182.46424\n  iter/sec; at 4,022,833 cycles this needs about 73.40 MHz. The forecast\n  is provisional until median timing establishes whether cycle savings\n  outweigh added frontend logic.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Add one fall-through buffer for instruction, PC and prediction,\n      available/capture control, independent request-PC advancement,\n      simultaneous consume/refill and reset/redirect cancellation.\n      Keep predictor lookup on the actual fetch request and split head\n      payload assignments from validity/recovery logic.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire physical imemReady to fetch, decoded-head availability to\n      the hazard unit, and selected head source indices to both hazard\n      and prospective forwarding comparisons. Preserve all backend\n      and RVFI wiring and the nret=1 port set.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Clarify or rename the imem-ready input to mean decode-head\n      availability. Retain late-result, execute-busy, data-memory hold\n      and recovery priorities, so buffered heads can issue during\n      physical instruction-bus stalls without losing backend interlocks.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Model the fetch request and buffered decode head independently;\n      verify FIFO order, response acceptance, saved predictions and\n      flushes. Update architecture-specific scheduling snapshots while\n      retaining architectural, operand, training, memory, divider-latency\n      and bounded-progress assertions. Add directed empty/full buffer,\n      refill, backpressure, dependency, reset and recovery cases.\n'\"''')\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nx=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(x,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and schema valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Updated and schema valid: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r10s1.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
