ard comparisons and\n  prospective forwarding tags MUST use the selected decode-head\n  instruction, not raw io_imemData, because the bus can now address\n  the following instruction. Keep head payload selection independent\n  of redirect/flush/validity. Use separate continuous assignments for\n  payload and validity so no artificial packed-bundle combinational\n  dependency feeds flush back into the source-index comparisons.\n\n  Let stall be the existing frontend stall output after the above\n  availability change. Outside \n…[5081 of 8153 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9908fca15c6ae759]…\nd-head availability to\n      the hazard unit, and selected head source indices to both hazard\n      and prospective forwarding comparisons. Preserve all backend\n      and RVFI wiring and the nret=1 port set.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Clarify or rename the imem-ready input to mean decode-head\n      availability. Retain late-result, execute-busy, data-memory hold\n      and recovery priorities, so buffered heads can issue during\n      physical instruction-bus stalls without losing backend interlocks.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Model the fetch request and buffered decode head independently;\n      verify FIFO order, response acceptance, saved predictions and\n      flushes. Update architecture-specific scheduling snapshots while\n      retaining architectural, operand, training, memory, divider-latency\n      and bounded-progress assertions. Add directed empty/full buffer,\n      refill, backpressure, dependency, reset and recovery cases.\nCounter({'PASS': 52})\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
