{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261001-002-r10s1|hyp-20261001-001-r7s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Replace the combinational divider with a bounded iterative execution unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, 12,312 LUT4s, and a 199.837 ns, 156-cell critical path through\\nforwarding and u_ex/u_alu. There are no prior structural attempts and no\\nLESSONS.md. The ALU currently synthesizes signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder as combinational / and % operators. These are the strongest\\nsuspected source of the very deep execute path; they constrain every\\ninstruction's clock period even when no division executes. Moving this\\narithmetic into a registered, shared unit should substantially improve\\nfrequency and area at the cost of extra cycles only for DIV/REM operations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, 12,312 LUT4s, and a 199.837 ns, 156-cell critical path through\\nforwarding and u_ex/u_alu. There are no prior structural attempts and no\\nLESSONS.md. The ALU currently synthesizes signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder as combinational / and % operators. These are the strongest\\nsuspected source of the very deep execute path; they constrain every\\ninstruction's clock period even when no division executes. Moving this\\narithmetic into a registered, shared unit should substantially improve\\nfrequency and area at the cost of extra cycles only for DIV/REM operations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU blocking multicycle EX operations using one\\nshared unsigned restoring divider that generates four quotient bits per\\ncycle. Keep the existing single-issue pipeline, combinational RV32I ALU,\\nand multiplier. Remove real combinational / and % from the synthesized\\ncore. This is one structural change: decouple long division from ordinary\\nsingle-cycle execution, without adding a cache, predictor, or wider issue.\\n\\nCapture the fully forwarded operands, operation, signedness, and RV\n…[127293 of 130365 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:54f4aa928dd0be3d]…\nses.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 180.21, \"delta_pct\": 3.31, \"vs_baseline\": 1386.88, \"fmax_mhz\": 72.497, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4022833, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5410, \"ff\": 1280, \"seeds\": [68.737, 72.497, 72.497], \"perturbations\": [[0, 68.737, 18], [1, 72.497, 18], [2, 72.497, 18]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/divisor_q_5_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_bank[1]_0_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -9.548, \"arrival_ns\": 19.842, \"logic_cells\": 29, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 18, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T14:19:41.842278Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r10s1 (regression, +3.31%): A one-entry fall-through fetch buffer raises CoreMark iterations/cycle by 5.15% by fetching during backend holds, but decode-head muxing and control fanout reduce Fmax enough to miss the 4.6% fitness-gain threshold.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
