{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"The refined two-entry queue reached 73.832 MHz and 185.46 iter/sec, a preliminary 6.32% gain over the champion. Simplifying payload capture while keeping validity checks separate recovered the frequency loss. I’ll make this the final hypothesis and check the exact refinement with formal and pipeline tests."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_44", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r11s1.yaml')\nd=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Two-entry elastic fetch queue with validity-independent payload capture'\ns=d['hypothesis']\na=s.index('Implement the ordinary payload')\nb=s.index('Compute\\\\npredictions',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''Separate payload capture from response acceptance and validity.\nThis detail is essential to the measured candidate. Let stall be the\nsame frontend hold above, response={request_pc,imem_data,prediction},\nand head_q/tail_q be packed 65-bit payload registers. Outside reset:\n  head_load = head_valid XOR stall;\n  tail_load = head_valid && (\"'!tail_valid || !stall);\n  if (head_load) head_q <= tail_valid ? tail_q : response;\n  if (tail_load) tail_q <= response.\nDo not qualify these wide payload enables with imemReady, fetch_accept,\nredirect or flush. They intentionally capture some invalid responses;\nvalidity alone determines whether a captured response may be consumed.\nWhen head is empty and decode holds, it may sample an unready response\nbut stays invalid; when a full queue is held, both payloads retain.\nOn consuming a full queue, head receives the valid tail while tail\nmay sample an unready response and become invalid. Capturing into an\ninvalid tail during a head-only dequeue is also harmless.\n\nFor occupancy, reset or redirect clears both valid bits. Otherwise,\nif !stall, set head_valid_next = head_valid &&\n(tail_valid || fetch_accept), tail_valid_next = tail_valid &&\nfetch_accept. Otherwise, if fetch_accept, set head_valid_next=1 and\ntail_valid_next=old_head_valid. Otherwise retain both valid bits.\nRequest PC reset/recovery retains highest priority; on a normal edge\nadvance it only on fetch_accept. Recovery installs redirect_target\nand flushes younger ID/EX validity, even if the instruction bus is\nstalled. Any same-edge wrong-path payload capture remains invalid.\nReset initializes both payload registers deterministically. Compute\npredictions'\"'''+s[b+len('Compute\\\\npredictions'):]\na=s.index('The initial seven-percent')\nb=s.index('Preserve existing test coverage',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''A prototype of exactly this two-entry fall-through queue with the\npayload enables above completed canonical stalled CoreMark in\n3,981,061 bracketed cycles, versus 4,230,003 for the champion, and\npassed the canonical CRCs, UART validation, marker and bounds checks.\nGowin placement options 0/1/2 measured 70.727,73.832,73.832 MHz,\nmedian 73.832 MHz. Preliminary fitness is 185.45810 iter/sec, a\n6.32-percent gain over 174.44, above the required 182.46424 threshold.\nOption-zero resources were 5,557 LUT4s, 1,346 registers, 40 LUT-RAMs,\nfour BSRAMs and two DSPs. The six-percent forecast rounds this result;\nreproduce it on implementation before claiming champion replacement.\n\nResponse-qualified, priority-selected payload writes in an otherwise\nidentical two-entry queue measured only 59.337 MHz, despite identical\nCoreMark cycles. Thus merely adding capacity is insufficient: retain\nthe simple payload equations and separate valid-bit discipline above.\nThe final refinement is undergoing formal and directed qualification;\ncomplete results and any limitations must be checked before acceptance.\nMain risks are synthesis/routing differences consuming the remaining\nmargin, incorrect invalid-payload handling, and regressions in saved\npredictions or retained forwarding across longer independent fetches.\n\n'''+s[b:]\nd['hypothesis']=s\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'medium'}\nd['changes'][0]['description']+='Use head_load=head_valid XOR stall and tail_load=head_valid && (\"'!tail_valid || !stall); do not gate payload enables with response-ready, fetch_accept or recovery. Keep valid-bit updates response-qualified.'\"\\\\n'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_style=None,width=78))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
