nd the\\\n  \\ predicted_taken\\nbit captured when that bus response was accepted. The request\\\n  \\ PC\\naddresses the next response, independently of the decode-head PC.\\n\\nDecode\\\n  \\ sees head when head_valid, otherwise the live response.\\nKeep this as one two-input\\\n  \\ payload mux; do not introduce an indexed\\nqueue read or a third tail input in\\\n  \\ the combinational decode path.\\nMove tail into head only across a clock edge.\\\n  \\ The valid states are\\nempty, head-only and head-plus-tail; tail_valid implies\\\n  \\ head_valid.\\nExport fetch_available = head_valid || io_imemReady to the hazard\\n\\\n  unit in place of physical instruction ready. Both late-use detection\\nand prospective\n…[7155 of 10227 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:68e579980dd4d95c]…\netch and logical head availability\n\n    to hazard control. Compare the selected decode instruction''s\n\n    source indices in both hazard and prospective forwarding units.\n\n    Preserve all backend wiring and the exact nret=1 external ports.\n\n    '\n- file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n  description: 'Interpret frontend ready as decode-head availability, retaining\n\n    existing dependency, divider, data-stall and recovery priorities.\n\n    Permit buffered decode during physical instruction-bus stalls\n\n    without coupling valid/flush back into payload comparisons.\n\n    '\n- file: test/test_pipeline.py\n  description: 'Extend the independent frontend reference model to a two-entry\n\n    queue and retain all architectural assertions while updating\n\n    obsolete lockstep fetch/decode timing snapshots. Add directed\n\n    occupancy transitions, simultaneous consume/refill, held tail,\n\n    dependency, saved prediction, reset and redirect tests with both\n\n    buses stalled; retain bounded progress and exact-once RVFI checks.\n\n    '\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
