{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261001-002-r1[012]s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Replace the combinational divider with a bounded iterative execution unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, 12,312 LUT4s, and a 199.837 ns, 156-cell critical path through\\nforwarding and u_ex/u_alu. There are no prior structural attempts and no\\nLESSONS.md. The ALU currently synthesizes signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder as combinational / and % operators. These are the strongest\\nsuspected source of the very deep execute path; they constrain every\\ninstruction's clock period even when no division executes. Moving this\\narithmetic into a registered, shared unit should substantially improve\\nfrequency and area at the cost of extra cycles only for DIV/REM operations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, 12,312 LUT4s, and a 199.837 ns, 156-cell critical path through\\nforwarding and u_ex/u_alu. There are no prior structural attempts and no\\nLESSONS.md. The ALU currently synthesizes signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder as combinational / and % operators. These are the strongest\\nsuspected source of the very deep execute path; they constrain every\\ninstruction's clock period even when no division executes. Moving this\\narithmetic into a registered, shared unit should substantially improve\\nfrequency and area at the cost of extra cycles only for DIV/REM operations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU blocking multicycle EX operations using one\\nshared unsigned restoring divider that generates four quotient bits per\\ncycle. Keep the existing single-issue pipeline, combinational RV32I ALU,\\nand multiplier. Remove real combinational / and % from the synthesized\\ncore. This is one structural change: decouple long division from ordinary\\nsingle-cycle execution, without adding a cache, predictor, or wider issue.\\n\\nCapture the fully forwarded operands, operation, signedness, and RV\n…[148790 of 151862 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:010c05fdc71d70a8]…\nter\\nsnapshots. Check all occupancies, full dequeue/enqueue, long holds,\\nper-source WB snooping, shift-edge writes, exact PC/prediction order,\\nflush/reset and no entry duplication or loss. Verify masks against\\nthe producer stages after each edge rather than mirroring RTL equations.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 176.4, \"delta_pct\": 1.12, \"vs_baseline\": 1355.45, \"fmax_mhz\": 70.141, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3976169, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6207, \"ff\": 1554, \"seeds\": [69.785, 70.141, 70.141], \"perturbations\": [[0, 69.785, 15], [1, 70.141, 15], [2, 70.141, 15]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/head_q.rs2_val_1_s1\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_1_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -9.33, \"arrival_ns\": 19.624, \"logic_cells\": 42, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T15:43:25.483735Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 12}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
