n\n  Supply independent asynchronous register reads for live instruction\n  source addresses and buffered-head source addresses. A straightforward\n  portable implementation is two reg_file instances receiving identical\n  clock, reset and actual WB writes; each instance provides two read\n  ports. Both copies must preserve x0 and same-cycle write-first bypass.\n  Select live versus saved-head register values only AFTER the reads,\n  using registered head occupancy. The queue stores source addresses,\n  not operand values. A held head therefore observes current architectural\n  registers on every cycle, including WB while the backend is held.\n  No snoop-update ports, operand version tags or new scoreboard are needed.\n  Allow synthesis to share storage if it preserves all four read functions.\n\n  Keep fixed head and tail slots. Decode uses saved head when valid,\n  otherwise the live response. Set fetch_available=head_valid||imemReady\n  and feed this logical availability to the existing hazard controller.\n  Source comparisons and prospective forwarding refer to the selected\n  instruction, never the next physical bus response. Preserve youngest\n  writer priority, the existing registered one-hot EX operand masks and\n  the load/multiply-use bubble. Payload selection must depend only on\n  occupancy, not redirect, flush or fetch validity.\n\n  Outside reset/recovery, let consume=\"'!stall, using the frontend hold\n  computed with logical fetch availability and existing backend hazards.\n  Accept a bus response when imemReady && (!tail_valid || consume).\n  Advance the request PC only on acceptance, predicting from that request\n  PC and its actual bus instruction. Empty consume bypasses directly into\n  ID/EX; empty hold saves the response in head. Head-only consume replaces\n  head with an accepted response or empties the queue; head-only hold\n  appends to tail. Full consume promotes tail and optionally refills tail;\n  full hold preserves both entries. Sustain one instruction per cycle\n  with ready buses, including simultaneous full consume/refill.\n\n  Separate wide payload writes from validity. With response denoting the\n  live predecoded payload, use head_load=head_valid ''^ stall and\n  tail_load=head_valid && (!tail_valid || !stall). On head_load, capture\n  tail_valid ? tail_payload : response; on tail_load capture response.\n  Do not qualify these payload enables with imemReady, redirect or flush.\n  Sampling an unready or wrong-path response into an invalid slot is safe;\n  a valid held slot must never be overwritten. For normal validity updates,\n  if !stall set head_valid_next=head_valid&&(tail_valid||fetch_accept)\n  and tail_valid_next=tail_valid&&fetch_accept. Otherwise, on acceptance,\n  set head_valid_next=1 and tail_valid_next=old_head_valid; otherwise hold.\n  Tail validity always implies head validity.\n\n  Reset empties the queue and initializes its payload deterministically.\n  Recovery overrides acceptance, clears both valid bits and younger\n  ID/EX validity, and installs redirect_target even during an instruction\n  bus stall. A same-edge speculative payload write remains invalid.\n  Save each accepted prediction; never recompute it on dequeue. Leave\n  exact direct targets, agree counters, training and JALR behavior intact.\n  Keep decode payload and source-index assignments separate from validity\n  assignments to avoid a combinational recovery/hazard feedback loop.\n\n  The isolated prototype preserves the expected 3,981,061 bracketed\n  CoreMark cycles, all canonical CRCs, validation text and memory bounds.\n  Selftest and three random programs pass full RVFI cosimulation both\n  with and without instruction/data stalls, eight passing trace cases.\n  Vendor timing and complete formal qualification must decide whether\n  the additional read ports and queue controls are worthwhile. At this\n  cycle count acceptance requires median Fmax above 72.640127 MHz and\n  fitness above 182.46424 iter/sec. The six-percent forecast is a target,\n  not a measured claim of an accepted replacement.\n\n  Main risks are extra register-file write fanout, replication area,\n  control/operand muxing before ID/EX, and the unchanged backend becoming\n  timing-limiting. Measure the median over all vendor placement options;\n  do not count pruned RVFI logic or a single favorable option as a gain.\n  Keep nret=1 ports, exact-once channel-0 RVFI order, all traps, original\n  real and ALTOPS arithmetic, nine-cycle division scheduling, stable\n  blocked memory requests and the unchanged formal liveness bound.\n\n  Validate the queue against an independent FIFO and architectural\n  register model, stressing writes while a head waits, same-edge WB and\n  dequeue, youngest producer overrides, x0, every occupancy transition,\n  both bus stalls, redirects at full occupancy, and reset. Run unchanged\n  formal, exact M-extension tests and canonical stalled CoreMark. Update\n  only obsolete frontend scheduling snapshots; preserve architectural,\n  arithmetic, progress and exact-once assertions.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Extend the fetch payload with validated decode controls and immediate;\n      retain raw instruction, PC and saved prediction. Do not buffer operand\n      values or change downstream architectural/RVFI payload meanings.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a two-entry fall-through head/tail buffer with live predecode,\n      independent request PC, logical availability, saved predictions and\n      validity-independent payload capture. Expose head instruction and\n      occupancy for the separate register-file read path; retain prediction\n      and recovery semantics.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Consume selected predecoded controls and immediate instead of decoding\n      after an instruction-head mux. Capture register values selected after\n      independent reads, preserving ID/EX enables, forwarding masks and\n      validity-only squash. Preserve source indices for RVFI.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Instantiate coherent live-response and buffered-head register-file\n      read copies with identical actual WB writes and reset. Select their\n      read outputs by head occupancy. Wire fetch availability to hazards\n      and selected instruction tags to hazards and prospective forwarding.\n      Preserve all backend datapaths and the exact nret=1 top-level ports.\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Treat frontend ready as selected-head availability, preserving late\n      result, divider, data-memory hold and recovery priorities. Document\n      that dependency indices refer to the selected instruction, not the\n      independently advancing physical fetch response.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Check buffered-head register reads against current committed state\n      and prospective forwarding during WB, backend holds and dequeue.\n      Cover same-rd writers, loads/multiplies, divider completion, branches,\n      stores and JALR under both bus stalls. Retain RVFI, bounded progress\n      and arithmetic assertions while updating obsolete fetch snapshots.\n  - file: test/test_if_queue.py\n    description: |\n      Add an independent accepted-instruction FIFO and register-value oracle.\n      Exercise all occupancies, full consume/refill, invalid live responses,\n      held payload stability, redirects, reset and saved predictions.\n      Check predecoded controls against the decoder'\"'s existing legality\n      tests and coherent read-copy behavior including WB write-first and x0.\nYAML\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r13s1.yaml')\nh=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert h['id']=='hyp-20261001-002-r13s1' and h['category']=='structural'\nprint('Replaced hypothesis and validated schema')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Replaced hypothesis and validated schema\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
