{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"ls -la .agents .codex; rg --files cores/bench/test; cat cores/bench/core.yaml; sed -n '1,100p' formal/checks_si.cfg; rg -n 'structural|r8s1|r9s1|r11s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c1-500\"", "aggregated_output": ".agents:\ntotal 8\ndr-xr-xr-x   2 hwebench hwebench   40 Oct  1 18:23 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 11 nobody   nogroup  4096 Oct  1 18:23 ..\n\n.codex:\ntotal 8\ndr-xr-xr-x   2 hwebench hwebench   40 Oct  1 18:23 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 11 nobody   nogroup  4096 Oct  1 18:23 ..\ncores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_mul_pipe.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 73.79\n  lut4: 5422\n  ff: 1214\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261001-002-r7s1\n  updated: '2026-10-01T12:32:29.027369Z'\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap;