{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r1s1 (improvement, +598.02%): Replacing combinational / and % in the ALU with a shared bounded iterative DIV/REM unit lets clock-period savings across all instructions outweigh the extra division cycles.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r1s2 (regression, +9.90%): Local saturating updates in the 128-entry bimodal table avoid a second indexed counter read mux and shared write-data fanout, raising median Gowin Fmax from 5.204 to 5.596 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r2s0 (regression, +14.79%): Capturing 3D once and using parallel D/2D/3D trial subtractions in div_unit.sv cuts serial subtract/select depth from four restoring bits to two radix-4 digits per cycle, gaining 14.79% fitness without adding DIV/REM cycles.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-002-r2s1 (improvement, +22.39%): Moving four narrow restoring steps into operand capture lets div_unit.sv register the unsigned result before sign correction, breaking the completion-path arithmetic cascade without extending nine-cycle DIV/REM occupancy.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r2s2 (regression, +9.83%): Exact B/J target prediction with a saved predicted_taken bit avoids the one-slot redirect bubble in combinational IF/ID, improving iterative-divider fitness to 92.92 but still trailing divider retiming at 103.54.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r3s0 (regression, +6.72%): Valid-bit-only fetch and ID/EX flushes improve fitness by removing redirect muxes from decode and operand capture, but raw load-use detection must use imem_ready rather than redirect-dependent IF validity.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r3s2 (improvement, +8.95%): A predictor that trails a newer champion can still improve it when combined: bimodal branch-slot savings compound with divider completion retiming when PC/validity-only recovery keeps late EX resolution out of decode, load-use detection, and ID/EX payload muxes.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r4s0 (regression, +2.43%): Direct magnitude prefixes and a nibble lookup in div_unit.sv shift the timing bottleneck to the unchanged full-width restoring chain and ALU-to-data-memory paths, limiting the gain to 2.43% at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r4s2 (improvement, +8.57%): Encoding backward-taken/forward-not-taken agreement in 64 locally updated counters halved predictor state and lookup mux fan-in while preserving CoreMark cycle performance, with the gain driven mainly by measured Gowin Fmax (47.405 to 51.374 MHz) rather than direction-miss reduction.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extens