eight iterations of four explicitly unrolled\nrestoring steps, each with a 33-bit trial remainder/subtraction, a quotient\nshift register, and a registered divisor. Select quotient or remainder and\napply the appropriate sign on the final iteration, transferring directly\ninto EX/MEM without an extra completion cycle. Budget at most nine EX\noccupancy cycles including operand capture. This bound is deliberate:\nwith ready buses, even a taken branch or load-use bubble immediately before\na division must leave at most ten cycles between retirements, satisfying\nthe unchanged liveness 1 10 20 check. Confirm this bound w\n…[19959 of 23031 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0a149e1ac36f519e]…\nisor shortcuts, and 135,748 full\nRV32M comparisons against integer division with truncation toward\nzero. These checks support the arithmetic decomposition only; RTL\nhandshake correctness and FPGA timing still require implementation.\n\nMeasure actual median Gowin Fmax times bracketed CoreMark iterations\nper cycle with canonical CRCs, UART validation, memory bounds and\nmarkers. Unchanged cycles are expected, not measured for this proposal.\nAcceptance requires fitness strictly above 117.99926, corresponding\nto approximately 49.5862 MHz at 4,202,246 cycles. The forecast of ten\npercent improvement is unmeasured; inspect vendor timing to confirm\nthat the operand-capture path was cut and preparation did not replace\nit with an equally slow path.\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r4s2 predictor improvement 122.48 51.374\n  path: {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -14.657, 'arrival_ns': 24.951, 'logic_cells': 13, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
