r the last\n  four phases. At a phase starting after c consumed bits, remainder is\n  bounded by the consumed dividend prefix, hence R < 2^c even for D=0.\n  For its j-th incoming bit, the trial fits w=c+j bits. Subtract the\n  low w bits of the captured divisor using an explicitl\n…[3045 of 6117 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fcf215a6abcf9751]…\nish a gain. Preserve nret=1 and all\n  correctness and evaluation contracts.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 10\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/div_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Repartition the seven recurrence cycles to consume 6,6,4,3,3,3,3\n      bits after the unchanged four-bit launch. Add explicitly bounded\n      early-phase restoring networks with full-divisor rejection and\n      share a three-step full-width network for the last four phases.\n      Preserve the external protocol, ninth-cycle transfer, registered\n      unsigned completion, sign correction and identical ALTOPS timing.\n  - file: test/test_div_unit.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve exact RV32M vectors and all handshake coverage. Update\n      prefix-state checks to consumed counts 4,10,16,20,23,26,29,32.\n      Add differential phase-boundary and high-divisor cases, especially\n      powers of two around each narrow step, plus reset and held-result\n      checks without relaxing the existing nine-cycle latency assertion.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
