{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category')=='structural':\n  print('\\\\nID',d['id'],'TITLE',d['title'],'OUTCOME',d.get('outcome'),'FITNESS',d.get('fitness'))\n  print('PATH',d.get('critical_path'))\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\nID hyp-20261001-002-r1s1 TITLE Replace the combinational divider with a bounded iterative execution unit OUTCOME improvement FITNESS 84.6\nPATH {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -20.478, 'arrival_ns': 30.772, 'logic_cells': 138, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nMake DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU blocking multicycle EX operations using one\nshared unsigned restoring divider that generates four quotient bits per\ncycle. Keep the existing single-issue pipeline, combinational RV32I ALU,\nand multiplier. Remove real combinational / and % from the synthesized\ncore. This is one structural change: decouple long division from ordinary\nsingle-cycle execution, without adding a cache, predictor, or wider issue.\n\nCapture the fully forwarded operands, operation, signedness, and RVFI\nmetadata exactly once when a valid division is accepted. Normalize signed\noperands at launch. Use eight iterations of four explicitly unrolled\nrestoring steps, each with a 33-bit trial remainder/subtraction, a quotient\nshift register, and a registered divisor. Select quotient or remainder and\napply the appropriate sign on the final iteration, transferring directly\ninto EX/MEM without an extra completion cycle. Budget at most nine EX\noccupancy cycles including operand capture. This bound is deliberate:\nwith ready buses, even a taken branch or load-use bubble immediately before\na division must leave at most ten cycles between retirements, satisfying\nthe unchanged liveness 1 10 20 check. Confirm this bound with directed\nsequences and formal; do not solve a failure by changing formal depths or\nshortening only the formal model's execution latency.\n\nHold fetch and ID/EX while a division occupies EX. Distinguish this hold\nfrom a data-memory stall: older EX/MEM and MEM/WB instructions must drain\nonce, and EX/MEM must receive a side-effect-free invalid bubble after an\nolder instruction advances while the divider is busy. A blocked memory\nrequest must instead retain its payload and current bu\n…[39042 of 42114 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4a6de03d958ea58e]…\nxisting wrapper_si.sv and checks_si.cfg properties/depths in\nisolated generated staging. Re-run these gates on the implementation.\nReal-arithmetic formal-deep was not run; retain real arithmetic tests\nbecause default formal substitutes ALTOPS for multiplication.\n\nA comparison prototype retaining the earlier low-half EX result reached\n69.558 MHz and 4,194,434 cycles, about 165.83 fitness. It offered no\nmeaningful fitness advantage and used 111 more LUT4s. Select the fully\nregistered reconstruction described above as this single hypothesis.\n\nReproduce and remeasure this register placement and result-availability\nschedule. Acceptance requires fitness strictly above 161.04216, or\n68.120882 MHz at the measured 4,230,003 cycles. The eight percent\nforecast rounds the preliminary measured gain; it is not a guarantee.\nMain risks are a non-multiply ALU path actually setting the clock,\nMEM reconstruction becoming critical, divider timing re-emerging,\nregister/routing cost and dependency bubbles outweighing Fmax gains.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
