{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\":\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"|hyp-20261001-00[123]-r[578]s[012]' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Replace the combinational divider with a bounded iterative execution unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, 12,312 LUT4s, and a 199.837 ns, 156-cell critical path through\\nforwarding and u_ex/u_alu. There are no prior structural attempts and no\\nLESSONS.md. The ALU currently synthesizes signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder as combinational / and % operators. These are the strongest\\nsuspected source of the very deep execute path; they constrain every\\ninstruction's clock period even when no division executes. Moving this\\narithmetic into a registered, shared unit should substantially improve\\nfrequency and area at the cost of extra cycles only for DIV/REM operations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, 12,312 LUT4s, and a 199.837 ns, 156-cell critical path through\\nforwarding and u_ex/u_alu. There are no prior structural attempts and no\\nLESSONS.md. The ALU currently synthesizes signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder as combinational / and % operators. These are the strongest\\nsuspected source of the very deep execute path; they constrain every\\ninstruction's clock period even when no division executes. Moving this\\narithmetic into a registered, shared unit should substantially improve\\nfrequency and area at the cost of extra cycles only for DIV/REM operations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU blocking multicycle EX operations using one\\nshared unsigned restoring divider that generates four quotient bits per\\ncycle. Keep the existing single-issue pipeline, combinational RV32I ALU,\\nand multiplier. Remove real combinational / and % from the synthesized\\ncore. This is one structural change: decouple long division from ordinary\\nsingle-cycle execution, without adding a cache, predictor, or wider issue.\\n\\nCapture the fully forwarded operands, operation, signedness, and RV\n…[157782 of 160854 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:baa7775d0b9336a7]…\n: -3.51, \"vs_baseline\": 1288.7, \"fmax_mhz\": 71.197, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4230003, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5356, \"ff\": 1247, \"seeds\": [68.731, 71.197, 71.197], \"perturbations\": [[0, 68.731, 13], [1, 71.197, 18], [2, 71.197, 18]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.read_data_5_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.raw_rs2_mask_2_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -9.55, \"arrival_ns\": 19.844, \"logic_cells\": 36, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_wb\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_fwd\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T13:02:01.743019Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r8s2 (regression, -3.51%): Separating predicted and recovery PC registers kept CoreMark cycles unchanged but moved the worst path to agree-counter training and reduced Gowin Fmax, showing that removing the late EX-to-PC input mux can merely relocate the timing bottleneck.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
