{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('category') == 'structural' or d.get('round_id',0)>=7:\n  print(d['id'], d.get('category'),d.get('title'), 'fitness=',d.get('fitness'),'MHz=',d.get('fmax_mhz'),'cycles=',d.get('cycles'))\n  print('critical:',d.get('critical_path'))\n  if d.get('category')=='structural':\n   h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n   s=h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h\n   print(s[:1600])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-002-r1s1 structural Replace the combinational divider with a bounded iterative execution unit fitness= 84.6 MHz= 37.999 cycles= 4491485\ncritical: {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -20.478, 'arrival_ns': 30.772, 'logic_cells': 138, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nMake DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU blocking multicycle EX operations using one\nshared unsigned restoring divider that generates four quotient bits per\ncycle. Keep the existing single-issue pipeline, combinational RV32I ALU,\nand multiplier. Remove real combinational / and % from the synthesized\ncore. This is one structural change: decouple long division from ordinary\nsingle-cycle execution, without adding a cache, predictor, or wider issue.\n\nCapture the fully forwarded operands, operation, signedness, and RVFI\nmetadata exactly once when a valid division is accepted. Normalize signed\noperands at launch. Use eight iterations of four explicitly unrolled\nrestoring steps, each with a 33-bit trial remainder/subtraction, a quotient\nshift register, and a registered divisor. Select quotient or remainder and\napply the appropriate sign on the final iteration, transferring directly\ninto EX/MEM without an extra completion cycle. Budget at most nine EX\noccupancy cycles including operand capture. This bound is deliberate:\nwith ready buses, even a taken branch or load-use bubble immediately before\na division must leave at most ten cycles between retirements, satisfying\nthe unchanged liveness 1 10 20 check. Confirm this bound with directed\nsequences and formal; do not solve a failure by changing formal depths or\nshortening only the formal model's execution latency.\n\nHold fetch and ID/EX while a division occupies EX. Distinguish this hold\nfrom a data-memory stall: older EX/MEM and MEM/WB instructions must drain\nonce, and EX/MEM must receive a side-effect-free invalid bubble after an\nolder instruct\nhyp-20261001-002-r2s1 structural Retime divider completion using first-nibble work during opera\n…[14098 of 17170 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:21529291186ab9aa]…\nove full-width 3D preparation onto the launch path.\n\nFor phase zero set C=3, N=5, P=8 and W=10. Begin with one binary\nrestoring step, followed by the existing two parallel-trial radix-4\ndigits. Form the W-bit first trial by zero-extending\n{R[0][2:0],Q[0][31]}, subtract zero-extended d1 using W+1 bits, select\nby borrow, and shift the quotient by one. Feed this intermediate\nquotient/remainder into two ordinary D/2D/3D radix-4 steps. Preserve\nthe existing 10-bit local d3 and the phase-wide D>=256 bypass; the\nbypass shifts Q[0] by five and appends its five high bits to R[0].\nLater phases retain their existing C,N,P,W values and\nhyp-20261001-003-r8s2 predictor Separate predicted and recovery PC registers without adding a miss cycle fitness= 168.31 MHz= 71.197 cycles= 4230003\ncritical: {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.read_data_5_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.raw_rs2_mask_2_s0', 'slack_ns': -9.55, 'arrival_ns': 19.844, 'logic_cells': 36, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_wb', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_fwd']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
