 5,422 and\n  1,214 for the champion; LUT RAM, BSRAM and DSP counts were unchanged.\n  Canonical CoreMark with both bus stalls retained exactly 4,230,003\n  marker-bracketed cycles, with all CRCs, validation text and bounds\n  checks passing. Calculated fitness is 175.72092 iter/sec, only\n  0.7343 percent above 174.44. This measured candidate DOES NOT exceed\n  the required 182.46424 acceptance threshold. The one-percent forecast\n  below reflects this small measured gain, not a claim of replacement.\n  Worst reported paths moved into existing forwarded ALU/address logic.\n\n  The prototype passed the unchanged real and ALTOPS divider suites and\n  existing real/ALTOPS pipeline suites, including independent prefix\n  arithmetic, captured operands, predictor behavior, exact-cycle checks,\n  reset, completion backpressure and the ten-cycle ready-bus retirement\n  bound. Selftest and three random programs passed full RVFI cosimulation\n  both with and without stalls, eight passing trace cases. Complete\n  formal qualification remains required; do not infer it from simulation\n  or alter the frozen checks to accommodate this change.\n\n  Preserve all existing tests. Add directed first-phase cases around\n  D=0,1,2,3,255,256,257 and signed equivalents, every two-bit launch\n  prefix, radix-4 decision boundaries, maximum first-byte prefixes and\n  large divisors whose low byte aliases a small divisor. Independently\n  check saved narrow 3D and the first successor Q/R state against the\n  captured magnitude and integer division. Cover request mutation,\n  reset and consecutive differing divisors. Reproduce the full vendor\n  median and validated CoreMark metric during implementation; retain\n  the champion unless the unchanged 4.6-percent threshold is exceeded.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 1\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/div_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Add resettable 10-bit prefix_triple_q, written only on accepted\n      launch from explicitly zero-extended divisor_magnitude[7:0].\n      Feed it directly to phase-zero d3. Preserve the full 34-bit\n      triple preparation during phase zero, later-phase arithmetic,\n      large-divisor bypasses, bit partition and all real/ALTOPS timing.\n  - file: test/test_div_unit.py\n    description: |\n      Retain exact arithmetic, per-bank prefix invariants and handshake\n      coverage. Add launch and phase-zero checks for the saved narrow\n      triple, D=255/256 boundaries, low-byte aliases of large divisors,\n      signed magnitudes, zero divisor, source mutation, reset and\n      consecutive requests. Keep the existing nine-cycle assertions.\n'''\np.write_text(content)\nd=yaml.safe_load(content)\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261001-002-r9s1'\nassert d['category']=='structural'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert -50<=d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']<=50\nprint('Final hypothesis written and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Final hypothesis written and schema-valid: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r9s1.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
