{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"The delayed-recovery prototype fails the unchanged bounded-liveness check: a redirect followed by DIV can exceed the permitted retirement gap. I’ll replace that proposal with one that preserves recovery latency and computes branch comparisons in parallel with forwarding selection."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_43", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r10s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-003-r10s2',\n'title':'Resolve branch predictions with comparisons parallel to forwarding',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion's reported worst path starts at a registered forwarding mask and ends at the fetch PC through EX branch resolution. Prior counter-table shrinking, Gray encoding and separate PC storage failed to clear the threshold. The existing checker selects 32-bit forwarded operands before comparing them, putting forwarding selection and comparison in series. Branch prediction recovery can instead select between precomputed one-bit outcomes, without extending recovery or changing the divider's already tight bounded-liveness schedule.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace the conditional-branch prediction checker in EX with parallel prospective-source comparisons followed by a one-bit selection. This is one predictor-recovery architecture change. Retain the existing 64-entry agree predictor, direct B/J targets, saved predicted_taken bit, single PC register, unpredicted JALR, and same-cycle EX recovery/training. No additional pipeline stage, miss cycle, table change or arithmetic-unit optimization is proposed.\n\nDefine the three rs1 candidates as in.rs1_val, fwd_ex_mem, fwd_mem_wb and the three rs2 candidates as in.rs2_val, fwd_ex_mem, fwd_mem_wb. Evaluate the decoded branch condition independently for every candidate pair before forwarding selection. Pair (i,j) is selected by in.raw_rs1_mask[i] AND in.raw_rs2_mask[j]. OR the nine pair outcomes masked by those enables to produce branch_cond. The existing one-hot masks retain younger-producer priority and choose exactly one pair for a valid instruction. Compare the original sources directly; never feed these predicate units from the already-muxed rs1/rs2 buses.\n\nEach pair evaluates BEQ/BNE, BLT/BGE and BLTU/BGEU with the exact existing signed and unsigned semantics; reserved branch_op values yield false. Express equality once and unsigned less-than once per pair, derive signed less-than from differing signs or unsigned less-than, and share complementary outcomes. Same-source EX/MEM-versus-EX/MEM and MEM/WB-versus-MEM/WB comparisons are constant equal and not-less; allow synthesis to fold them. Keep the shallow selected-outcome OR explicit. Do not replace the source masks, create an indexed operand mux ahead of a shared comparator, or impose a new reset, valid or WB-write-enable gate on forwarded data.\n\nKeep ordinary forwarded rs1/rs2 and independent ALU operand selection unchanged for ALU, JALR, stores, multiply/divide, and RVFI. Use the selected branch_cond in the existing branch_taken, actual_taken, redirect and train_agree equations without changing any qualification or latency. Direct target arithmetic and alignment checks remain unchanged. A correct prediction still accepts its successor without a bubble; a direction miss still squashes exactly the current fetched instruction on the same advancing EX cycle. Preserve deferred resolution during older dmem stalls, divider holds, recovery priority over imem stalls, valid-only flushing and MEM/WB data retention.\n\nThe expected benefit is moving the wide compare alongside forwarding selection rather than after it, shortening the path from the saved forwarding controls into prediction checking, PC recovery and predictor training. Multiple comparisons cost area and increase source-data fanout; unchanged divider and ALU paths may then limit the clock. The initial forecast is a 5 percent fitness gain with low confidence, principally from Fmax at unchanged CoreMark cycles. This is a hypothesis, not a demonstrated qualifying improvement. Accept only measured median Gowin Fmax times canonical CoreMark iterations/cycle above 182.46424 iterations/second; at 4,230,003 cycles that needs about 77.183 MHz.\n\nA separate exploratory prototype with a registered recovery boundary was rejected because an extra recovery cycle followed by division failed the unchanged bounded-liveness check. Do not adopt delayed recovery or relax that check. This proposal preserves the champion's recovery and division latencies and targets only the combinational prediction-checking path.\n\nPreserve nret=1, all top-level ports and RVFI fields, decoder legality, misalignment traps, exact-once retirement, memory handshakes, real and ALTOPS arithmetic, and every invariant. Prove combinational equivalence of selected branch_cond to comparing the original forwarded operands for all operand values, all branch_op values and all nine legal one-hot source combinations. Run the existing pipeline predictor and operand monitors unchanged, the unchanged formal suite and full-RVFI cosim, then canonical stalled CoreMark validation and all three Gowin placement options.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Compute branch predicates for every prospective rs1/rs2 forwarding-source pair in parallel, then select the one-bit result using the existing registered one-hot raw masks. Share equality, signed/unsigned ordering and complements within pairs; fold identical-source cases. Preserve all other execution, recovery, training, target, trap and pipeline-enable equations and every arithmetic datapath.'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Keep existing predictor counter, recovery timing, exact-cycle, operand and architectural assertions unchanged. Add directed branches covering every legal condition and all nine forwarding source combinations, including identical-source pairs, younger-over-older writer priority, x0, signed extrema and unsigned high-bit cases. Exercise both prediction outcomes, load/multiply-use bubbles, held dmem forwarding, simultaneous imem stalls, completed division and misaligned taken targets. Check exact RVFI operands/PCs, once-only training, no wrong-path memory effects and unchanged retirement progress.'''}]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent(dumper,s):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s or len(s)>110 else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,represent)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\nimport json,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Replaced and schema-validated:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
