ective-source comparisons followed by a one-bit selection. This is one predictor-recovery architecture change. Retain the existing 64-entry agree predictor, direct B/J targets, saved predicted_taken bit, single PC register, unpredicted JALR, and same-cycle EX recovery/training. No additional pipeline stage, miss cycle, table change or arithmetic-unit optimization is proposed.\n\n  Define the three rs1 candidates as in.rs1_val, fwd_ex_mem, fwd_mem_wb and th\n…[3642 of 6714 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9fe81a67609cacb4]…\n for every prospective rs1/rs2 forwarding-source pair in parallel, then select the one-bit result using the existing registered one-hot raw masks. Share equality, signed/unsigned ordering and complements within pairs; fold identical-source cases. Preserve all other execution, recovery, training, target, trap and pipeline-enable equations and every arithmetic datapath.\n- file: test/test_pipeline.py\n  description: |-\n    Keep existing predictor counter, recovery timing, exact-cycle, operand and architectural assertions unchanged. Add directed branches covering every legal condition and all nine forwarding source combinations, including identical-source pairs, younger-over-older writer priority, x0, signed extrema and unsigned high-bit cases. Exercise both prediction outcomes, load/multiply-use bubbles, held dmem forwarding, simultaneous imem stalls, completed division and misaligned taken targets. Check exact RVFI operands/PCs, once-only training, no wrong-path memory effects and unchanged retirement progress.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
