{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_82", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema,textwrap\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r10s2.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Parallel branch predicates for same-cycle predictor recovery'\nh=d['hypothesis']; a=h.index('Define three rs1 candidates:'); b=h.index('\\\\n\\\\nEach candidate comparison',a)\nh=h[:a]+'''Define three rs1 candidates as in.rs1_val, fwd_ex_mem and fwd_mem_wb, and three rs2 candidates as in.rs2_val, fwd_ex_mem and fwd_mem_wb. Evaluate the decoded branch condition independently for every candidate pair before forwarding selection. Pair (i,j) is selected by in.raw_rs1_mask[i] AND in.raw_rs2_mask[j]. OR the nine pair outcomes masked by those enables to produce branch_cond. The existing one-hot masks retain younger-producer priority and choose exactly one pair for a valid instruction. Compare the original sources directly; never feed the predicate units from already-muxed rs1 or rs2 buses.''' +h[b:]\nh=h.replace('Each candidate comparison evaluates','Each pair evaluates').replace('once per candidate comparison','once per pair')\na=h.index('The expected benefit is'); b=h.index('\\\\n\\\\nPreserve nret=1',a)\nh=h[:a]+'''The intended benefit is moving the wide compare alongside forwarding selection, shortening the path from saved forwarding controls into prediction checking, PC recovery and predictor training. Multiple comparisons cost area and increase source-data fanout; unchanged divider and ALU paths can limit the clock. Preserve the original recovery latency: adding a recovery stage can violate the unchanged bounded-liveness check on a redirect to DIV.\n\nAn isolated nine-pair prototype passed all 53 unchanged nret=1 ALTOPS formal checks, the 38 existing pipeline tests plus their multiply ALTOPS runner, and full-RVFI comparison of selftest and three random programs both with and without bus stalls. A combinational SAT proof established exact branch-condition equivalence for every operand value, every branch_op, and every legal pair of one-hot forwarding masks. Canonical stalled CoreMark retained exactly 4,230,003 marker-bracketed cycles, all five CRCs, validation text, completion and in-bounds operation.\n\nThat prototype measured 66.254, 71.444 and 71.444 MHz across Gowin placement options 0/1/2, median 71.444 MHz. Option zero used 5,755 LUT4s and 1,214 registers with unchanged LUT RAM, BSRAM and DSP counts. Calculated fitness is 168.89704 iterations/second, about 3.18 percent below the 174.44 champion. The limiting paths include forwarded ALU/data-memory and fetch recovery. Thus this tested implementation does NOT qualify; the forecast records its measured limitation. The three-comparison variant using already-forwarded rs2 was worse and is not proposed.\n\nRetain the champion unless the final implementation's measured median Gowin Fmax times canonical CoreMark iterations/cycle exceeds 182.46424 iterations/second. At unchanged 4,230,003 cycles, this requires Fmax above 77.18243 MHz. Do not change arithmetic units, the table, verification gates or benchmark to compensate for this predictor experiment's timing limitations.''' +h[b:]\nd['hypothesis']=h;d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']=-3\nd['changes'][0]['description']='Compute branch predicates for all nine prospective rs1/rs2 forwarding-source pairs in parallel, then select the one-bit result with the existing registered one-hot raw masks. Share equality, signed/unsigned ordering and complements within each pair; identical EX/MEM-versus-EX/MEM and MEM/WB-versus-MEM/WB source pairs are constant. Preserve every other execution, recovery, training, target, trap and pipeline-enable equation and all arithmetic datapaths.'\nfor k in ['motivation','hypothesis']:d[k]='\\\\n\\\\n'.join(textwrap.fill(x,78) for x in d[k].split('\\\\n\\\\n'))+'\\\\n'\nfor c in d['changes']:c['description']=textwrap.fill(c['description'],76)+'\\\\n'\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\nD.add_representer(str,lambda dumper,s:dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None))\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=90));jsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Schema valid. Nine-pair projected fitness:',71.444*1e7/4230003)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
