{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_29", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 -B - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r11s2.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261001-003-r11s2\ntitle: \\\"Select the recovery target from the saved branch prediction\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's reported worst path runs from the registered forwarding\n  mask through EX branch resolution into the fetch PC. Profiling canonical\n  CoreMark finds only 13,735 JALRs and approximately 46,342 conditional\n  direction misses, too few for better accuracy alone to provide a reliable\n  4.6-percent fitness gain. Prior counter shrinking and parallel predicate\n  experiments also failed to clear the threshold. The current recovery\n  datapath unnecessarily uses the late actual_taken result both to detect\n  a miss and to select its 32-bit destination.\nhypothesis: |\n  Decouple direct-branch recovery target selection from the actual branch\n  outcome. Because the existing direct predictor uses exact B/J targets,\n  on a direction miss the correct successor is precisely the alternative\n  to the saved prediction. In EX compute redirect_target as\n  in.ctrl.is_jalr ? jump_target :\n  in.predicted_taken ? (in.pc + 32'd4) : branch_target.\n  Keep the existing branch_target and jump_target arithmetic. All target\n  selection controls are then ID/EX register outputs; the late forwarded\n  branch comparison only controls whether recovery occurs, rather than\n  also steering the 32-bit recovery data. This is one predictor-recovery\n  datapath change with no added stage, table, register or recovery cycle.\n\n  Preserve redirect = advancing && (actual_taken \"'!= in.predicted_taken),\n  every advancement qualification, actual_taken, misalignment handling,\n  branch training and the actual EX/MEM pc_next calculation. Retain the\n  64-entry agree predictor, saved predicted_taken, exact aligned B/J\n  prediction and unpredicted JALR. A predicted-not-taken direct branch\n  that actually takes recovers to branch_target; a predicted-taken branch\n  that falls through recovers to PC+4. JALR remains unpredicted and selects\n  the real forwarded jump_target. Aligned JAL is correctly predicted;\n  faulting direct transfers are never predicted taken and retain the\n  current trap/linear-PC behavior. The redirect_target bus may differ\n  when redirect is false, because no consumer accepts it in that case.\n  Do not feed the new counterfactual recovery target into RVFI pc_next.\n\n  Keep valid-only squash, PC recovery priority over instruction-bus stalls,\n  deferral under data-memory stalls and execute holds, and all current\n  decode/hazard/forwarding behavior. Do not add actual_taken as a fallback\n  selector, which would recreate the path being removed. Do not narrow\n  addresses, add register stages or modify arithmetic units. Preserve\n  nret=1, decoder legality, all RVFI and memory behavior, ALTOPS, exact-once\n  retirement and the unchanged bounded-progress checks.\n\n  Verify the selected recovery address equals the architectural next PC\n  whenever redirect is asserted for every reachable prediction/transfer\n  combination. Retain architectural and predictor tests, adapting only\n  assertions that inspect an unused redirect_target when redirect is low.\n  Run the unchanged formal and full-RVFI cosimulation gates, then canonical\n  stalled CoreMark and all three Gowin placement options. With unchanged\n  4,230,003 cycles, passing the 4.6-percent threshold requires median Fmax\n  above 77.18243 MHz and fitness above 182.46424 iter/sec. The initial gain\n  estimate is an unmeasured forecast; remaining comparator, divider and\n  ALU paths may limit the improvement.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Select direct recovery data from the saved predicted_taken bit,\n      choosing PC+4 for predicted-taken and branch_target otherwise, with\n      a registered-control JALR override to the actual jump_target. Keep\n      the redirect condition, real pc_next, alignment/trap decisions,\n      predictor training, branch arithmetic and all other execution logic.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise both direct direction-miss cases, correct predictions,\n      JAL, JALR, misaligned and illegal transfers, forwarded branch operands,\n      simultaneous instruction stalls, held data-memory operations and\n      divider completion. Assert redirect_target against architectural\n      next PC whenever redirect is asserted; retain exact-cycle prediction,\n      counter training, RVFI, operand, memory and progress checks.\n'\"''')\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Refined hypothesis validates')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
