     choosing PC+4 for predicted-taken and branch_target otherwise, with\n      a registered-control JALR override to the actual jump_target. Keep\n      the redirect condition, real pc_next, alignment/trap decisions,\n      predictor training, branch arithmetic and all other execution logic.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Exercise both direct direction-miss cases, correct predictions,\n      JAL, JALR, misaligned and illegal transfers, forwarded branch operands,\n      simultaneous instruction stalls, held data-memory operations and\n      divider completion. Assert redirect_target against architectural\n      next PC whenever redirect is asserted; retain exact-cycle prediction,\n      counter training, RVFI, operand, memory and progress checks.\n'\"''')\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Refined hypothesis validates')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Refined hypothesis validates\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"The refinement targets recovery timing: on a direct-branch misprediction, the correct destination is already determined by the saved prediction. Selecting that destination early removes one late branch-outcome mux from the fetch-PC path. An isolated prototype is running through simulation and Gowin timing."}}
