ression, +9.90%): Local saturating updates in the 128-entry bimodal table avoid a second indexed counter read mux and shared write-data fanout, raising median Gowin Fmax from 5.204 to 5.596 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-001-r2s0 (regression, +14.79%): Capturing 3D once and using parallel D/2D/3D trial subtractions in div_unit.sv cuts serial subtract/select depth from four restoring bits to two rad\n…[5848 of 8920 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:be8887afb17b99fe]…\n0 (regression, +1.75%): Preselecting final MEM/WB writeback_data and registering forwarded rs1 + imm as EX/MEM effective_addr improved timing together where either alone regressed, but shifted the bottleneck to branch/predictor training, limiting unchanged-cycle CoreMark gains to 1.75%, below the 4.6% acceptance margin.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r11s2 (regression, +0.00%): Registering predicted_taken ? PC+4 : predicted_target as recovery_pc removes late actual_taken from direct recovery address selection, but the isolated prototype lost 2.97% fitness at unchanged CoreMark cycles because the first divider recurrence became timing-limiting.\n- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r12s2 (regression, +0.83%): Pairing separate predicted/recovery PC registers with delayed banked agree-counter training addresses both competing EX feedback sinks without adding CoreMark cycles, but shifts the timing limit to forwarded load data through the ALU into data memory, leaving only a 0.83% fitness gain below the acceptance margin.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
