{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|return.address|return stack|RAS|gshare|history' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Replace the combinational divider with a bounded iterative execution unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, 12,312 LUT4s, and a 199.837 ns, 156-cell critical path through\\nforwarding and u_ex/u_alu. There are no prior structural attempts and no\\nLESSONS.md. The ALU currently synthesizes signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder as combinational / and % operators. These are the strongest\\nsuspected source of the very deep execute path; they constrain every\\ninstruction's clock period even when no division executes. Moving this\\narithmetic into a registered, shared unit should substantially improve\\nfrequency and area at the cost of extra cycles only for DIV/REM operations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, 12,312 LUT4s, and a 199.837 ns, 156-cell critical path through\\nforwarding and u_ex/u_alu. There are no prior structural attempts and no\\nLESSONS.md. The ALU currently synthesizes signed and unsigned division and\\nremainder as combinational / and % operators. These are the strongest\\nsuspected source of the very deep execute path; they constrain every\\ninstruction's clock period even when no division executes. Moving this\\narithmetic into a registered, shared unit should substantially improve\\nfrequency and area at the cost of extra cycles only for DIV/REM operations.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU blocking multicycle EX operations using one\\nshared unsigned restoring divider that generates four quotient bits per\\ncycle. Keep the existing single-issue pipeline, combinational RV32I ALU,\\nand multiplier. Remove real combinational / and % from the synthesized\\ncore. This is one structural change: decouple long division from ordinary\\nsingle-cycle execution, without adding a cache, predictor, or wider issue.\\n\\nCapture the fully forwarded operands, operation, signedness, and RV\n…[335567 of 338639 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d9d97dfdc4843cf2]…\n \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4230003, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5418, \"ff\": 1259, \"seeds\": [72.382, 74.396, 74.396], \"perturbations\": [[0, 72.382, 12], [1, 74.396, 13], [2, 74.396, 13]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.read_data_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -8.816, \"arrival_ns\": 19.11, \"logic_cells\": 12, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_wb\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 12, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T15:23:59.638132Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r12s2 (regression, +0.83%): Pairing separate predicted/recovery PC registers with delayed banked agree-counter training addresses both competing EX feedback sinks without adding CoreMark cycles, but shifts the timing limit to forwarded load data through the ALU into data memory, leaving only a 0.83% fitness gain below the acceptance margin.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
