{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r14s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-003-r14s2',\n'title':'Isolate conditional-branch resolution from prospective forwarding',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The existing prediction policy already leaves limited accuracy headroom: an\narchitectural CoreMark trace contains 46,342 conditional misses and 13,735\nJALRs inside the markers. Recent predictor storage changes did not improve\nbackend-limited Fmax. Inspection reveals a less obvious feedback path:\nmisalign_fault includes the forwarded conditional-branch comparison and\nsuppresses ctrl_with_trap.reg_write, which then drives next_reg_write and\nthe prospective forwarding masks captured for the following instruction.\nA conditional branch cannot write a register, so this control dependency\nis unnecessary for every decoder-reachable instruction.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Separate branch-trap reporting from jump link-write suppression in EX.\nKeep misalign_branch, misalign_jump and misalign_fault unchanged, and set\nctrl_with_trap.is_illegal on their existing OR. Clear reg_write only for\nmisalign_jump; a legal or faulting conditional branch already arrives with\nreg_write=0 from the unchanged decoder. Keep next_reg_write qualified by\nin.valid and this corrected ctrl_with_trap.reg_write. Thus conditional\nbranch comparison and its prediction outcome no longer enter prospective\nregister-writer qualification through the trap-control mux. Preserve JAL\nand JALR link suppression for misaligned targets exactly.\n\nThis is one predictor-resolution feedback isolation change, with no\nprediction-policy or recovery-latency change. Keep the 64-entry agree\npredictor, local counter transitions, training timing, exact B/J targets,\nsaved direction bit, unpredicted JALR, PC selection and validity-only\nsquashes unchanged. The desired timing effect is removal of a forwarded\noperand -> conditional comparison -> branch fault -> writer enable ->\nprospective source-mask register path, and lower comparator fanout. Do\nnot change the ALU, divider, multiplier, register file or memory interface.\n\nThe equivalence relies on the real decoder's is_branch implying both\n\"'!reg_write and !is_jump, an invariant that must be explicitly checked,\nincluding reserved branch encodings and reset/hold behavior. Do not drop\nany trap or misalignment check: a taken misaligned branch still traps and\nstays sequential, a not-taken misaligned branch does not trap, and a\nmisaligned JAL/JALR still traps without writing its link register. Keep\nnret=1, all RVFI fields, monotonic order and the original progress bounds.\n\nThe forecast is unmeasured and low-confidence. Other ALU and divider\npaths may remain limiting, as they did in prior predictor attempts.\nValidate architectural equivalence with unchanged formal and full RVFI\ncosim, plus directed branch/jump fault and forwarding tests. Run canonical\nstalled CoreMark with all CRCs, bounds, markers and validation text, and\nmeasure all three Gowin placement options. Accept only if median Fmax\ntimes iterations/cycle exceeds 182.46424 iterations/second; at unchanged\n4,230,003 cycles this requires more than 77.18243 MHz.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Keep branch/jump fault generation and trap reporting unchanged. Separate\nreg_write suppression from the combined misalign_fault condition and\napply it only to misalign_jump, so conditional-branch resolution cannot\nfeed next_reg_write or EX/MEM writer control through this path. Preserve\nall actual targets, redirects, training and architectural metadata.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_decoder.py','description':'''Add an exhaustive encoding-level property for conditional branches:\naccepted branch controls never assert reg_write or is_jump, and reserved\nbranch funct3 encodings remain illegal and have no write enable. Retain\nall existing decoder-default and SYSTEM legality checks.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Cover each branch condition in taken/not-taken and aligned/misaligned\ncases with forwarded operands, younger dependent writes, and both bus\nstalls. Check misaligned JAL/JALR link suppression, branch trap/sequential\nPC behavior and no wrong-path memory or register effects. Preserve the\nexisting predictor oracle, exact retirement ordering and ten-cycle\nready-bus progress checks; pipeline scheduling should remain identical.'''}]}\nclass D(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef represent(d,s):return d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nD.add_representer(str,represent)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=D,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Revised hypothesis written and schema validated.')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
