{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('category')=='predictor':\n  print(d['id'],d['title'])\n  print(d.get('implementation_notes','')[:5500])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-003-r1s2 Small bimodal predictor with immediate direct targets\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r2s2 Recover branch bubbles with a stall-safe bimodal predictor\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r3s2 Bimodal prediction with a short validity-only recovery path\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r4s2 Compact 64-entry agree predictor with backward/forward branch bias\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r5s2 Register bank-decoded training events for the 64-entry agree predictor\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r6s2 Eight-entry folded-PC agree predictor with local saturating updates\n# Eight-entry folded-PC agree predictor\n\nImplemented the proposed predictor in `cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv`,\n`ex_stage.sv`, and `core.sv`. The bank contains exactly eight independent\nbinary two-bit counters, reset to `2'b10`, with local saturating updates.\nFetch selects only the counter MSB using `pc[4:2] ^ pc[7:5]`; EX trains using\nthe resolving instruction's `in.pc[4:2] ^ in.pc[7:5]`. Both interfaces and\nthe core training wire are three bits. `train_valid` and `train_agree` are\nunchanged. No architectural deviations from the proposed RTL change.\n\nUpdated the independent cycle-level predictor oracle in\n`cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py` to eight counters and folded indices.\nAdded directed tests for eight PCs spaced 32 bytes apart that separate after\nfolding, and all 64 combinations of the two three-bit address fields.\nAdapted deliberate collision chains to PCs 16/52/88 and destructive\nopposite-bias aliases to PCs 16/52. Retained the 256-byte alias test.\nChecks cover both saturation limits, concurrent lookup/update with pre-edge\nprediction, all counter contents on every edge, reset, held/squashed\ninstructions, exact-once training/retirement, legality/alignment, metadata\nholds, memory backpressure, and divider behavior. Existing architectural,\noperand, and cycle-stamped regression assertions remain enabled.\n\n## Local validation\n\n- Required Verilator lint command: PASS, no warnings or errors.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test`: PASS, seven runners, 101 cocotb cases,\n  including 34 pipeline cases and real/ALTOPS\n…[2593 of 5665 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:015e3599707fda0f]…\nrcent gain does not establish an\naccepted replacement or a robust five-percent improvement.\n\nOnly the three predictor RTL files, the pipeline test file, and this\nrequested implementation note were edited. Decoder, arithmetic, hazards,\npipeline metadata, RVFI ports/order, nret=1, and evaluation contracts were\npreserved.\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r7s2 Single-bit agree prediction in native distributed RAM\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r8s2 Separate predicted and recovery PC registers without adding a miss cycle\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r9s2 Compact 32-entry Gray-encoded agree predictor\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r10s2 Parallel branch predicates for same-cycle predictor recovery\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r11s2 Register the alternate successor for direct-branch recovery\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r12s2 Register both predictor feedback sinks without adding recovery latency\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r13s2 Split agree-predictor direction flops from RAM-backed confidence\n\nhyp-20261001-003-r14s2 Register predictor recovery with separate successor targets and a recovery barrier\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
