{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nids=['hyp-20261001-003-r8s2','hyp-20261001-003-r10s2','hyp-20261001-003-r11s2','hyp-20261001-003-r12s2','hyp-20261001-001-r9s0']\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if d.get('id') in ids:\n  print(d['id'])\n  print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261001-003-r8s2\nReplace the single fetch-PC storage register with two 32-bit registers,\npredicted_pc_q and recovery_pc_q, plus one recovery_active_q bit. The\narchitectural fetch PC is a combinational selection between these registers:\npc = recovery_active_q ? recovery_pc_q : predicted_pc_q. Use this selected\nPC consistently for imem_addr, out.pc, PC-relative prediction arithmetic\nand the unchanged agree-table index. Keep IF/ID combinational, ID/EX and\nEX resolution unchanged, and preserve the actual accepted predicted_taken\nbit. This is one predictor-recovery storage architecture change.\n\nOn reset set both PC banks to RESET_PC and recovery_active_q to zero.\nOtherwise, when !stall, capture the existing next_pc in predicted_pc_q.\nCapture redirect_target in recovery_pc_q whenever !recovery_active_q OR\nredirect. Thus the inactive correction bank can sample EX without a late\nredirect-dependent enable, while an active correction bank holds its PC\nthrough arbitrary instruction or pipeline stalls. A new redirect always\npermits capture, even when the correction bank is already active.\nSet recovery_active_q to one when redirect is asserted; otherwise clear\nit on !stall and retain it on a stall. Reset has highest priority and\nredirect has priority over stall for the bank selector and correction\ncapture. These are separate clocked assignments, not a reconstruction\nof the original three-way next-PC mux ahead of either bank.\n\nA resolving miss captures its target and selects the correction bank on\nthe SAME edge that currently updates the single PC register. The target\nis therefore visible during the same next cycle, with no new miss bubble,\npending execution operation or delayed branch retirement. If the target\nfetch stalls, keep the correction bank selected and stable. Once that\nfetch is accepted, capture its predicted successor in predicted_pc_q and\nselect that bank on the same edge. A predicted-bank write during a redirect\nis harmless because the correction bank becomes selected. Inactive-bank\nsampling must never chang\n…[23034 of 26106 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:812b7293d7c2dae6]…\non-policy timing expectations only where delayed training\nactually changes the predicted direction. The isolated prototype passed\nall 38 pipeline cases and six ALTOPS multiply pipeline cases after adapting\nthe independent event oracle. Preserve the lookup/update crossing assertion\nwith a directed cold forward-taken branch to an alias at PC+256, so lookup\ncoincides with the delayed weak-agree to weak-disagree write. Selftest and\nall three random programs passed full RVFI comparison both with and without\nstalls, eight cases total. All 53 unchanged single-retirement ALTOPS formal\nchecks also passed, including register consistency, PC continuity, unique\nretirement, legality and liveness. These ran in isolated staging with the\noriginal wrapper, properties and depths. Real-arithmetic formal-deep was\nnot run; arithmetic is unchanged. Reproduce these formal and full-RVFI\ncosim gates and canonical CoreMark CRC, UART, bounds and marker validation\non the final implementation before evaluating all three vendor options.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
