{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_93", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r15s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261001-003-r15s2\ntitle: \"Precompute alternate successors and isolate predictor recovery bank writes\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's reported worst path runs from registered forwarding\n  selection through EX into the fetch PC. Predictor accuracy has little\n  remaining cycle headroom: r14s2 recorded 46,342 conditional misses and\n  13,735 JALRs against 4,230,003 CoreMark cycles. R11s2 precomputed the\n  alternate successor but retained the late PC write mux; r12s2 separated\n  PC banks and delayed training but retained late recovery-address\n  selection. Neither cleared the acceptance margin. The opportunity is\n  to remove both data selection and wide write-enable fanout from direct\n  prediction recovery without adding a recovery cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Give predictor recovery an early address and a late one-bit selector.\n  Keep the 64-entry two-bit agree predictor, PC[7:2] indexing, exact\n  aligned B/J prediction, combinational IF/ID and unpredicted JALR.\n  In IF compute alternate_pc = predicted_taken ? PC+4 : predicted_target.\n  Capture this full-width address with the instruction in ID/EX under\n  its ordinary payload enable, holding it through stalls. In EX expose\n  recovery_target = is_jalr ? resolved_jump_target : alternate_pc.\n  Keep resolved architectural pc_next, actual_taken, alignment faults\n  and the qualified direction-mismatch redirect unchanged.\n\n  Replace IF's single PC register with predicted_pc_q, recovery_pc_q\n  and recovery_active_q. Select the visible PC with recovery_active_q,\n  and use that PC consistently for the address, prediction and metadata.\n  Capture predicted_pc_q = next_pc whenever !stall. Capture\n  recovery_pc_q = recovery_target whenever !recovery_active_q, with\n  NO redirect-dependent enable. Set recovery_active_q on redirect;\n  otherwise clear it when !stall and hold it on stall. Reset both\n  addresses to RESET_PC and clear recovery_active_q. Reset has priority.\n  A miss selects the already independent correction bank on the same\n  edge as the champion, wi\n…[3339 of 6411 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:aa21dc950d106841]…\nsuccessor, implement separate prediction and\n      recovery PC banks with registered ownership and no late redirect\n      in the correction-bank enable, and queue training by one cycle.\n      Preserve the existing counter implementation and lookup policy.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture and hold alternate_pc with the ordinary ID/EX payload.\n      Continue flushing only validity and prediction metadata.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive recovery_target from the saved alternate successor for direct\n      transfers and the existing resolved target for JALR. Preserve\n      mismatch qualification, traps, architectural pc_next and execution.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Add independent selected-PC recurrence and recovery-bank ownership\n      checks, and a one-event-delayed binary-counter oracle. Exercise\n      stalls, recovery, JALR, reset and branch-to-DIV progress without\n      weakening existing architectural or exact-once assertions.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
