{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"The trace changes the choice: the current predictor misses only about 54,500 of 529,588 conditional branches, and there are just 13,735 indirect jumps. That leaves little cycle savings for a larger predictor. A 32-entry bimodal table had nearly the same accuracy, so I’m investigating a smaller predictor that could preserve throughput while improving FPGA timing."}}
