d multiplier. Remove real combinational / and % from the synthesized\\ncore. This is one structural change: decouple long division from ordinary\\nsingle-cycle execution, without adding a cache, predictor, or wider issue.\\n\\nCapture the fully forwarded operands, operation, signedness, and RV\n…[107300 of 110372 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:570ad6a17b42acf7]…\n902.72, \"fmax_mhz\": 50.975, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4194434, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3197, \"ff\": 751, \"seeds\": [50.713, 50.975, 50.975], \"perturbations\": [[0, 50.713, 12], [1, 50.975, 24], [2, 50.975, 24]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -14.719, \"arrival_ns\": 25.013, \"logic_cells\": 12, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 12, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T10:55:04.155493Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r5s2 (regression, -0.78%): Registering eight-bank training decode for the 64-entry agree predictor saved 80 LUT4s but left CoreMark cycles unchanged and the critical path in register-file/forwarding and EX arithmetic, so predictor retiming did not improve the limiting path and median Fmax fell from 51.374 to 50.975 MHz.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
