{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_25", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r6s2.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-003-r6s2',\n'title':'Fold PC indexing to halve the agree predictor without losing branch coverage',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The current champion uses 64 locally updated two-bit agreement counters\nindexed by PC[7:2]. Prior training retiming left cycles unchanged and\nregressed timing. Smaller direct-index tables were also unsuccessful on\nthe previous champion, so simply repeating that downsizing is not the\nproposal. XOR folding upper PC bits changes which branches interfere,\nallowing a smaller table to preserve useful prediction coverage while\nreducing counter state, update decoding and lookup mux fan-in.\n\nAn independent interpreter profile of the canonical timed region found\n2,922,016 instructions, 529,588 conditional branches and only 13,735 JALR\nreturns. Thus a return stack offers too little cycle headroom. Architectural\ntrace replay produced 46,325 misses for the current 64-entry agree table,\n51,983 for a directly indexed 32-entry table, and 47,224 for the proposed\n32-entry folded table. These are direction-model counts, not cycle-accurate\nRTL results; actual stalled cycles and vendor timing remain decisive.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Replace the current 64x2 agree predictor with exactly 32 two-bit counters,\nusing fetch_index = pc[6:2] XOR pc[11:7]. Apply the identical five-bit\nfold to the resolving branch's own in.pc for train_index. This is a single\npredictor capacity/indexing change: fold two adjacent word-address fields\nso static branch sites separated by 128 bytes do not inevitably collide,\nwhile halving the state and prediction selection width. Use these ordinary\naddress bits for all programs; no hard-coded branch PCs, program signatures,\nbenchmark phase detection, or instruction-specific lookup contents.\n\nKeep agreement with backward-taken/forward-not-taken bias: each counter\nresets to 2'b10, increments with saturation when the resolved direction\nagrees with the B-immediate sign, and decrements otherwise. Each entry\nretains its own local transition and decoded update enable. Fetch reads\nonly the selected counter MSB, and the actual predicted direction is\ncounter[1] == imem_data[31]. Preserve legal-branch predecode, exact aligned\nB/J targets and unconditional aligned JAL prediction; JALR remains resolved\nin EX. Do not introduce a shared training read/modify/write mux, history,\na target table, delayed updates, new pipeline stages or speculative state.\n\nNarrow train_index to five bits consistently in IF, EX and core wiring.\nTrain exactly once per valid, legal, non-faulting conditional branch\nadvancing out of EX with \"'!stall, !execute_busy and !reset. Index the current\nlocal counter state with that branch'\"'s folded PC, never the fetch PC or a\nstale fetch-time counter snapshot. Simultaneous lookup/update observes the\npre-edge prediction; ordinary nonblocking counter update semantics suffice.\nDo not train on held branches, invalid slots, jumps, traps or wrong-path\nfetches. No bypass from the training event to the current prediction.\n\nKeep the saved actual predicted_taken bit, one-bit direction-mismatch\nrecovery, exact direct targets and architectural RVFI pc_next unchanged.\nPreserve reset/redirect/accept/hold PC priority, raw fetch instruction and\nsource-index paths, validity-only squashes, load-use interlocks, memory\nbackpressure, retained forwarding operands and divider scheduling. No\nchanges to arithmetic, decoder legality, ALTOPS, nret=1, external IO,\nretirement ordering or any evaluation contract are part of this hypothesis.\n\nThe prospective timing benefit comes from removing 64 counter flops and\nhalving both the direction mux and local-update population, at the cost of\nfive XOR functions on lookup and training indices. Accuracy replay suggests\nonly 899 additional misses in ten iterations versus the current table,\nroughly 0.02 percent of its 4,194,434 measured cycles if every extra miss\ncost one cycle. This estimate excludes pipeline/update and bus-stall phase\neffects. The unchanged divider is the reported critical path, so area\nreduction does not itself establish a frequency improvement; added hashing\nand placement perturbations are material risks.\n\nForecast five percent fitness improvement with low confidence pending the\nprototype. Measure canonical stalled CoreMark and the median of all three\nGowin placement options, not just a single favorable timing result. Require\nfitness strictly above 147.03622 iter/sec, 4.6 percent over 140.57. Validate\nall unchanged formal and architectural cosim gates, canonical CRCs and\nUART text, memory bounds, marker-bracketed cycles and forward progress.\nExtend the independent predictor oracle and directed alias tests to prove\nlookup/training use the same fold, exact-once updates, saturation, pre-edge\nread/write behavior and metadata retention under stalls and recovery.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':5,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Reduce agreements and local counters from 64 to 32 entries. Index the\nfetch MSB with pc[6:2] XOR pc[11:7], narrow train_index to five bits and\nuse five-bit per-entry comparisons. Retain local binary saturation,\nweak-agreement reset, prediction eligibility, immediate targets and\nall PC/validity priorities without adding training latency.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Narrow train_index to five bits and drive it from in.pc[6:2] XOR\nin.pc[11:7]. Preserve train_valid, train_agree and every existing\nbranch-resolution, recovery, arithmetic, hold and RVFI behavior.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Narrow the shared EX-to-IF train_index signal to five bits, matching\nboth module interfaces. Preserve all other interconnect and external IO.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Update the independent prediction oracle to 32 counters and the folded\nindex. Adapt predictor-specific alias addresses and expected states\nwhile preserving existing architectural assertions. Add pairs that\ncollide in low PC bits but separate under folding, pairs that collide\nonly after folding, opposite-bias aliases, every index, saturation,\nsame-index concurrent lookup/update, reset and held/squashed branches.\nRetain all legality, alignment, bus-stall, divider and RVFI coverage.\n'''}]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef string(d,s): return d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,string)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Wrote and validated',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
