arrow the training index consistently to\nthree bits in IF, EX and core wiring.\n\nPreserve binary counter encoding and reset every counter to 2'b10, weak\nagreement with backward-taken/forward-not-taken bias. Increment locally\nwith saturation when branch_taken equals the B-immediate sign, decrement\notherwise. Fetch reads only the selected MSB. For a legal conditional\nbranch with an aligned exact target, predicted_taken remains counter[1]\n== imem_data[31]. Retain the existing legal-branch predecode, unconditional\naligned JAL prediction, unpredicted JALR and exact B/J target adder. Do not\nadd history, tags, a target table, a return stack, delayed training, new\npipeline stages, or a shared indexed training read/modify/write datapath.\n\nTrain exactly once per valid legal non-faulting conditional branch\nadvancing out of EX under the unchanged \"'!reset, !stall and !execute_busy\nconditions. Use that branch'\"'s folded PC and the current local counter;\nnever use the fetch PC or a saved counter snapshot. A simultaneous lookup\nand update uses the pre-edge prediction and ordinary nonblocking update\nsemantics. Bubbles, held instructions, jumps, traps and squashed fetches\ncannot train. Keep train_agree and train_valid logic unchanged.\n\nCarry the same actual predicted_taken bit through the existing pipeline.\nExact direct targets still permit the existing one-bit mismatch recovery.\nPreserve reset/redirect/accept/hold PC priority, validity-only squashes,\nraw instruction and source-index paths, ID/EX metadata holds, load-use\ninterlocks, divider scheduling, memory backpressure and retained forwarding\noperands. Leave all arithmetic, ALTOPS behavior, decoder legality, nret=1,\ntop-level IO, architectural RVFI fields/order and evaluation contracts\nunchanged. No core_pkg or additional hazard logic changes are required.\n\nThe isolated prototype completed canonical CoreMark with both bus stalls\nin 4,221,451 marker-bracketed cycles, versus 4,194,434 for the champion:\n27,017 additional cycles, or approximately 0.64 percent. Both markers,\nall five expected CRCs, required UART validation text and no out-of-bounds\naccesses were observed. Gowin placement options 0/1/2 measured 59.219,\n59.924 and 59.924 MHz; median Fmax is 59.924 MHz versus 58.96 MHz. Option-0\narea was 3,212 LUT4s and 590 registers versus 3,501 and 702, with 40 LUT\nRAMs, four BSRAMs and six DSPs. Its worst reported path runs from retained\nMEM/WB load data through forwarding into divider launch; the arithmetic\npaths remain the limiting concern.\n\nCalculated prototype fitness is 141.95119 iter/sec, approximately 0.983\npercent above 140.57. This DOES NOT clear the required 147.03622 iter/sec\nacceptance threshold. At the measured cycle count, acceptance would require\nmedian Fmax above 62.07062 MHz. Forecast one percent with low confidence,\nnot an unsupported five percent gain. These are preliminary timing and\nCoreMark results, not completed formal qualification or an accepted\nreplacement. The prototype changes a real predictor circuit; nevertheless,\nits timing gain is too small to distinguish confidently from placement\nsensitivity under the tournament's acceptance rule.\n\nAfter implementation, reproduce actual bracketed cycles and median Gowin\nFmax, run unchanged formal and architectural cosim gates, and retain all\ncanonical CRC, UART, bounds, liveness and RVFI checks. Update the independent\nprediction oracle to eight counters and the three-bit fold. Add directed\nlow-index conflicts that separate after folding, deliberate folded\ncollisions, every index, opposite-bias aliases, saturation, same-index\nconcurrent lookup/update, reset and held/squashed branch cases. Retain all\nexisting architectural assertions and imem/dmem/divider stall coverage.\nPrincipal risks are increased interference in the very small table,\nworkload sensitivity and an unchanged divider-limited Fmax ceiling.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':1,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Reduce agreements and the generated local counter bank from 64 to eight\nentries. Select with pc[4:2] XOR pc[7:5], narrow train_index to three\nbits and compare each entry with a three-bit constant. Preserve binary\nsaturation, weak-agreement reset, immediate targets and PC/validity rules.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Narrow train_index to three bits and drive it from in.pc[4:2] XOR\nin.pc[7:5], matching fetch. Leave train_valid, train_agree, branch\nresolution, recovery, alignment, arithmetic, holds and RVFI unchanged.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Narrow the EX-to-IF train_index wire to three bits to match both\nmodule interfaces; preserve all remaining wiring and external ports.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Update the independent reference predictor to eight counters and the\nthree-bit folded lookup/training index. Adapt predictor-specific alias\naddresses and expected counter states without relaxing architectural\nassertions. Cover all indices, old low-bit conflicts that separate,\nnew fold collisions, opposite biases, saturation, pre-edge lookup/update,\nreset, stalled and squashed updates, metadata holds and exact-once\nretirement. Retain legality, alignment, bus and divider coverage.\n'''}]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef string(d,s): return d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,string)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert h['id']=='hyp-20261001-003-r6s2' and h['category']=='predictor'\nassert type(h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert -50 <= h['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct'] <= 50\nprint('Schema-valid final hypothesis:',p)\nPY\n git diff --exit-code -- cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/test\n g