immediate target adder and legal-branch predecode.\nUse precisely 64 entries and direct PC[7:2] indexing; no PC hash, history\ntable, target cache, return stack, or extra pipeline register is needed.\n\nRetain per-entry local saturating transitions with a decoded update enable:\nincrement toward 2'b11 on agreement, decrement toward 2'b00 on disagreement.\nFetch reads only the selected counter MSB. Keep training independent of an\nindexed counter read and shared read-modify-write datapath. The table uses\n128 state bits instead of 256 and a 64:1 direction selection instead of\n128:1. Oppositely biased branches can share an entry constructively when\neach usually follows its own bias, lim\n…[5578 of 8650 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:83bafdf13d3bd71f]…\n text. Calculated fitness was 121.5301 iter/sec,\n0.78 percent BELOW 122.48. This prototype therefore does not establish\nan improvement and does not clear the 128.11408 acceptance threshold.\nThe forecast is deliberately negative rather than claiming an unsupported\nfive-percent gain. This is the best completed predictor-only candidate\nfrom the investigation, not a measured winning replacement.\n\nAfter implementation, reproduce the median Gowin measurement and run the\nunchanged formal and architectural cosim gates. The preparation experiment\nwas a timing/CoreMark prototype, not a completed formal qualification.\nThe main limitation is that the measured critical path still traverses\nregister-file/forwarding and execute arithmetic outside the predictor;\ntraining retiming may not improve that limiting path sufficiently.\n\nnotes \n\nID hyp-20261001-003-r6s2 title Eight-entry folded-PC agree predictor with local saturating updates\nresults {'fitness': 141.82, 'cycles': 4221451, 'fmax_mhz': 59.867, 'lut4': 3262, 'ff': 590}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
