{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_59", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r8s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261001-003-r8s2',\n 'title':'Separate predicted and recovery PC registers without adding a miss cycle',\n 'category':'predictor',\n 'motivation':'''The champion's reported worst path starts at ID/EX raw_rs1_mask and ends\nat the fetch PC, through EX and IF, after multiplier pipelining raised\nmedian Fmax to 73.790 MHz. Prior table shrinking, training retiming and\none-bit RAM storage did not produce an accepted improvement. Keep the\nsuccessful 64-entry, two-bit agree predictor and improve its recovery\nintegration: the current PC register merges forwarded EX correction data,\nnormal predicted next-PC data and hold feedback at its input. Separate\nstorage for prediction and correction can remove this shared input mux\nfrom the late EX target path without paying another misprediction cycle.''',\n 'hypothesis':'''Replace the single fetch-PC storage register with two 32-bit registers,\npredicted_pc_q and recovery_pc_q, plus one recovery_active_q bit. The\narchitectural fetch PC is a combinational selection between these registers:\npc = recovery_active_q ? recovery_pc_q : predicted_pc_q. Use this selected\nPC consistently for imem_addr, out.pc, PC-relative prediction arithmetic\nand the unchanged agree-table index. Keep IF/ID combinational, ID/EX and\nEX resolution unchanged, and preserve the actual accepted predicted_taken\nbit. This is one predictor-recovery storage architecture change.\n\nOn reset set both PC banks to RESET_PC and recovery_active_q to zero.\nOtherwise, when \"'!stall, capture the existing next_pc in predicted_pc_q.\nCapture redirect_target in recovery_pc_q whenever !recovery_active_q OR\nredirect. Thus the inactive correction bank can sample EX without a late\nredirect-dependent enable, while an active correction bank holds its PC\nthrough arbitrary instruction or pipeline stalls. A new redirect always\npermits capture, even when the correction bank is already active.\nSet recovery_active_q to one when redirect is asserted; otherwise clear\nit on !stall and retain it on a stall. Reset has highest priority and\nredirect has priority over stall for the bank selector and correction\ncapture. These are separate clocked assignments, not a reconstruction\nof the original three-way next-PC mux ahead of either bank.\n\nA resolving miss captures its target and selects the correction bank on\nthe SAME edge that currently updates the single PC register. The target\nis therefore visible during the same next cycle, with no new miss bubble,\npending execution operation or delayed branch retirement. If the target\nfetch stalls, keep the correction bank selected and stable. Once that\nfetch is accepted, capture its predicted successor in predicted_pc_q and\nselect that bank on the same edge. A predicted-bank write during a redirect\nis harmless because the correction bank becomes selected. Inactive-bank\nsampling must never change the selected PC or create an instruction\nacceptance, predictor training event or architectural side effect.\n\nPreserve the existing PC next-state recurrence exactly: reset selects the\nreset vector; a redirect selects redirect_target regardless of imem stall;\notherwise an accepted fetch selects its predicted next PC; otherwise the\nselected PC holds. Do not rely on redirect and recovery_active_q being\nmutually exclusive. Retain the explicit redirect capture case so even this\ncombination is correct. Leave raw imem data and source-index paths,\nvalidity-only flushes, downstream stall qualification and recovery priority\nunchanged. All counter lookup/update ordering, legal B/J predecode,\nalignment suppression, JAL prediction and unpredicted JALR remain identical.\nNo target comparison, BTB, return stack, history table or pipeline register\nstage is added. Keep nret=1, all IO, RVFI, decoder, memory, arithmetic and\nALTOPS contracts unchanged.\n\nThe intended timing split is EX target arithmetic into the dedicated\ncorrection register, then a small registered-selector mux at fetch address.\nNormal prediction arithmetic feeds its own register without the late EX\ncorrection data input. The bank selector is only one bit. Expect roughly\n33 additional storage bits before synthesis, rather than a second complete\ninstruction packet. The important risk is that moving a mux after the PC\nregister adds delay to PC-to-imem/decode and PC-relative prediction paths,\nor an unchanged divider/ALU path becomes the frequency limit. Measure\nGowin timing; RTL mux counting alone cannot establish an improvement.\n\nUse the existing independent predictor/operand oracle and retain all exact\ncycle checks: ready-bus miss latency, prediction hit throughput, division\nschedule and retirement gaps must remain unchanged. Add directed bank\ntransition checks for reset, redirect coincident with imem-not-ready,\nseveral stalled cycles while a correction PC is active, release into both\nsequential and predicted-taken successors, consecutive control transfers,\nforwarded JALR targets, opposite-direction misses and training/read aliases.\nCheck selected-PC hold on data stalls and divider holds, exact-once\nretirement and memory effects, illegal/misaligned transfers and arbitrary\ninactive-bank values. Run unchanged formal, full RVFI cosim and canonical\nCoreMark validation with both bus stalls and marker-bracketed cycles.\n\nAcceptance requires fitness above 182.46424 iter/sec. If the champion'\"'s\n4,230,003 CoreMark cycles are preserved, median Fmax must exceed\n77.182428 MHz. The forecast is provisional until the isolated prototype's\nGowin timing and correctness checks finish; do not claim the architecture\nis a measured improvement without those results.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n  {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Introduce predicted and correction PC banks with a registered selector.\nImplement reset, independent bank captures, correction-over-stall priority\nand active-bank hold as specified. Drive all fetch PC uses from the selected\nbank while preserving existing prediction, training and validity behavior.'''},\n  {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain the independent predictor model and all existing exact-cycle,\narchitectural and progress assertions. Add directed selected-PC/bank\ntransition checks under reset, simultaneous redirect and imem stall,\nheld correction fetches, predicted successors, aliases, forwarding,\ndivider/data holds and squashed side effects.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90,default_flow_style=False))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and schema-valid:',p)\nprint('required MHz',174.44*1.046*4230003/1e7)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
