register\nstage is added. Keep nret=1, all IO, RVFI, decoder, memory, arithmetic and\nALTOPS contracts unchanged.\n\nThe intended timing split is EX target arithmetic into the dedicated\ncorrection register, then a small registered-selector mux at fetch address.\nNormal prediction arithmetic feeds its own register without the late EX\ncorrection data input. The bank selector is only one bit. Expect roughly\n33 additional storage bits before synthesis, rather than a second complete\ninstruction packet. The important risk is that moving a mux after the PC\nregister adds delay to PC-to-imem/decode and PC-relative prediction paths,\nor an unchanged divider/ALU path becomes the frequency limit. Measure\nGowin timing; RTL mux counting alone cannot establish an improvement.\n\nUse the existing independent predictor/operand oracle and retain all exact\ncycle checks: ready-bus miss latency, prediction hit throughput, division\nschedule and retirement gaps must remain unchanged. Add directed bank\ntransition checks for reset, redirect coincident with imem-not-ready,\nseveral stalled cycles while a correction PC is active, release into both\nsequential and predicted-taken successors, consecutive control transfers,\nforwarded JALR targets, opposite-direction misses and training/read aliases.\nCheck selected-PC hold on data stalls and divider holds, exact-once\nretirement and memory effects, illegal/misaligned transfers and arbitrary\ninactive-bank values. Run unchanged formal, full RVFI cosim and canonical\nCoreMark validation with both bus stalls and marker-bracketed cycles.\n\nAcceptance requires fitness above 182.46424 iter/sec. If the champion'\"'s\n4,230,003 CoreMark cycles are preserved, median Fmax must exceed\n77.182428 MHz. The forecast is provisional until the isolated prototype's\nGowin timing and correctness checks finish; do not claim the architecture\nis a measured improvement without those results.''',\n 'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n 'changes':[\n  {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Introduce predicted and correction PC banks with a registered selector.\nImplement reset, independent bank captures, correction-over-stall priority\nand active-bank hold as specified. Drive all fetch PC uses from the selected\nbank while preserving existing prediction, training and validity behavior.'''},\n  {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain the independent predictor model and all existing exact-cycle,\narchitectural and progress assertions. Add directed selected-PC/bank\ntransition checks under reset, simultaneous redirect and imem stall,\nheld correction fetches, predicted successors, aliases, forwarding,\ndivider/data holds and squashed side effects.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90,default_flow_style=False))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and schema-valid:',p)\nprint('required MHz',174.44*1.046*4230003/1e7)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
