{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_75","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r8s2.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['hypothesis']=d['hypothesis'].replace('The forecast is provisional until the isolated prototype\\\\'s\\\\nGowin timing and correctness checks finish; do not claim the architecture\\\\nis a measured improvement without those results.', '''An isolated prototype of this exact split-PC design measured Gowin Fmax\nof 67.836, 70.355 and 70.355 MHz across placement options 0/1/2: median\n70.355 MHz. CoreMark took exactly 4,230,003 marker-bracketed cycles with\nboth bus stalls, matching the champion, and passed canonical CRC, UART,\nbounds and marker validation. Calculated fitness is 166.32376 iter/sec,\n4.65274 percent below 174.44, so this prototype DOES NOT meet acceptance.\nThe negative-five-percent forecast reflects this measured regression;\ndo not present the original timing rationale as an observed speedup.\n\nThe prototype passed all 53 unchanged nret=1 ALTOPS formal checks,\nincluding liveness, register consistency, PC continuity, legality and\nunique retirement, using isolated staging of the original wrapper and\ncheck properties/depths. All 38 existing pipeline tests passed unchanged,\nincluding exact-cycle checks and the independent predictor/operand oracle.\nSelftest and three random programs passed full RVFI cosimulation both\nwith and without bus stalls, eight passing cases. Real-arithmetic\nformal-deep was not run; no arithmetic logic changes in this proposal.\n\nPlacement option zero used 5,431 LUT4s and 1,247 registers versus 5,422 and\n1,214 for the champion, with 40 LUT RAMs, four BSRAMs and two DSPs unchanged.\nIts reported worst path now ends at an agree counter, not a PC register;\noptions one and two likewise end in counter training. The PC-bank change\ntherefore moves the reported limiting path, but the remaining feedback and\narithmetic timing does not yield a net frequency improvement. Submit this\none bounded predictor-recovery hypothesis with that limitation explicit.\nReproduce the implementation and its full metric before any acceptance;\nretain the champion unless the unchanged threshold is actually exceeded.''')\nd['expected_impact']={'fitness_delta_pct':-5,'confidence':'low'}\nclass BlockDumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef string_repr(dumper,text):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',text,style='|' if '\\\\n' in text else None)\nBlockDumper.add_representer(str,string_repr)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=BlockDumper,sort_keys=False,width=90,default_flow_style=False))\nr=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());jsonschema.validate(r,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert r['id']=='hyp-20261001-003-r8s2' and r['category']=='predictor'\nassert type(r['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert -50<=r['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']<=50\nassert all(c['file'].startswith(('rtl/','test/test_')) for c in r['changes'])\nprint('Validated final hypothesis:',p)\nprint('Proposed files:',[c['file'] for c in r['changes']])\nPY\ngit status --short\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
