ubble in combinational IF/ID, improving iterative-divider fitness to 92.92 but still trailing divider retiming at 103.54.\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261001-003-r3s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Bimodal prediction with a short validity-only recovery path\",\n  \"fitness\": 112.81,\n  \"delta_pct\": 8.95,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 47.405,\n  \"cycles\": 4202246,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_0_s1\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -16.85,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 27.145,\n    \"logic_cells\": 26,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r3s2 (improvement\n…[4656 of 7728 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0d0d70f1457631a2]…\n    \"slack_ns\": -8.89,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 19.184,\n    \"logic_cells\": 38,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"lesson\": null\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261001-003-r8s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Separate predicted and recovery PC registers without adding a miss cycle\",\n  \"fitness\": 168.31,\n  \"delta_pct\": -3.51,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 71.197,\n  \"cycles\": 4230003,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.read_data_5_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.raw_rs2_mask_2_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -9.55,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 19.844,\n    \"logic_cells\": 36,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_wb\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_fwd\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-01 hyp-20261001-003-r8s2 (regression, -3.51%): Separating predicted and recovery PC registers kept CoreMark cycles unchanged but moved the worst path to agree-counter training and reduced Gowin Fmax, showing that removing the late EX-to-PC input mux can merely relocate the timing bottleneck.\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
